    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Illustration_R-02842": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Illustration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Illustration Compensation: $55,000-$62,000 Department: School of Art Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The School of Art at Ball State University welcomes applications for a full-time, tenure-line Assistant Professor of Illustration to teach undergraduate courses in illustration, animation, drawing, and other areas of interest and expertise. The ideal candidate will be a creative teacher, thoughtful mentor, and collaborative colleague. The School of Art has forty-five full-time faculty and staff and offers state-of-the-art facilities serving approximately 700 undergraduate majors. Programs at the BA, BS, and BFA levels include art education, art history, graphic design, graphic design studies, animation production, illustration, game art/design, visual effects, and a studio art program that includes drawing, painting, printmaking, ceramics, glass, metals + jewelry, sculpture, photography, and video and new media. School of Art students enjoy world-class facilities, with over 73,000 square feet of classroom, gallery, and studio space in the Art and Journalism Building, Applied Technology Building, and the Marilyn K. Glick Center for Glass. Students and faculty work closely with David Owsley Museum of Art on campus, among the finest university art collections in the nation. Ball State University is accredited by the National Association for Schools of Art and Design. Teaching responsibilities are on campus, in Muncie, Indiana. This position is open until filled with a priority consideration date of November 1, 2026. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Description:  Tenure-line faculty in the School of Art teach undergraduate courses at all levels, from first-year Foundations through senior projects. They also pursue creative and scholarly research in their field by exhibiting, publishing, and presenting their work professionally. All faculty participate in service at the School, College, and University level and are committed to student success and curricular innovation.     Duties and Responsibilities:  Courses are generally scheduled on campus, with occasional courses scheduled online, either synchronously or asynchronously.  ·        Instructional load will include all levels of course work in classes such as AFA 101 Drawing Studio, ART 213 Introduction to Illustration, ART 214 Surface Illustration, ART 317 Book Works, ART 318 Comic Art, and ART 417 Editorial Illustration. ·        Other teaching duties based on programmatic need and the expertise of the faculty hired individual may be assigned. ·        Additional responsibilities include course development, mentoring students at all levels, and supervising senior capstone projects. ·        Tenure-line faculty are also responsible for producing scholarship/creative work commensurate with the requirements for tenure. ·        The successful candidate will also be expected to contribute to and participate in the life and development of the School of Art, the College of Fine Arts, and the University by serving on committees and being active in their discipline’s community. Minimum Qualifications:  ·        MFA degree in illustration, animation, art, or related field from an accredited institution by date of appointment or at least six years of documented professional experience in illustration, animation, art, or related field.       Preferred Qualifications:  ·        Significant industry experience in the field of illustration  ·        Evidence of current professional practice in   illustration  ·        Experience and/or interest in developing new curriculum in illustration  ·        At least one year of teaching experience at the college level, gained concurrently or at any time. How to apply: For inquiries regarding this opportunity, please contact:  Lara Kuykendall, Director,  lkuykendall@bsu.edu      Please follow upload instructions to attach one PDF of all of the required supporting documents listed below. NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume. Cover Letter  Resume/Curriculum Vitae  Sample syllabus for one college-level illustration course Portfolio of up to 10 images of applicant’s creative work (with links to time-based work if applicable). If document size exceeds 10 MB, a link to portfolio may be provided.  Contact information (including email addresses) for three professional references  This position is open until filled with a priority consideration date of NOVEMBER 1, 2026. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration.  (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Police-Officer_R-03149": {
      "title": "Police Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Police Officer Compensation: $29.44 - $30.61 Department: Public Safety_H Start Date: 10/26/2026 About this opportunity: This position is open to both Tier 1 Certified applicants and Non-Certified applicants. The starting rate range is $29.44 to $30.61 per hour. Additionally, there is a $7,500 sign-on bonus for Tier 1 Certified applicants with a minimum of two years qualifying experience. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Perform functions related to the preservation of public peace and order, the prevention and detection of crime, the apprehension of offenders, the protection of persons and property, the enforcement of laws of the State of Indiana and the ordinances of the City of Muncie, the enforcement of rules and regulations of Ball State University, and the safeguarding of individual and collective rights of the citizenry. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Properly operate and maintain acceptable levels of proficiency in the use of department issued or approved equipment. Requires the physical ability to exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Requires the physical fitness level that meets current criminal justice standards. Requires the physical ability to sit for extended periods of time and drive patrol vehicles. Requires the ability to run, jump, stand, and walk for long periods of time, and the ability to physically subdue an offender with reasonable force and have reasonable strength to perform necessary lifesaving functions. Task requires a wide field of vision and the visual ability to perceive depth and distinguish colors. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to read, write, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information, and to receive, comprehend and follow oral instructions and information. Requires the mental ability to analyze problem situations and adjust to varying work assignments, use judgment and discretion, and demonstrate appropriate written and verbal communication skills. Task requires use of vehicles, bicycles, pistols, long guns, shot guns, chemical spray, impact weapons, knives, and any other tool used as a defensive weapon. Task requires use of Automated External Defibrillator and the ability to perform  CPR . 2. Patrol campus and university property by vehicle and on foot; conduct building and security checks; report any unusual or suspicious conditions. May require the physical ability to exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Requires the physical fitness level that meets current criminal justice standards. Requires the physical ability to sit for extended periods of time and drive patrol vehicles. Requires the ability to walk for long periods of time, and may require the ability to run, jump, stand, and physically subdue an offender with reasonable force and have reasonable strength to perform necessary lifesaving functions. Task requires a wide field of vision and the visual ability to perceive depth and distinguish colors. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to read, write, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information, and to receive, comprehend and follow oral instructions and information. Requires the mental ability to analyze problem situations and adjust to varying work assignments, use judgment and discretion, and demonstrate appropriate written and verbal communication skills. Task requires use of vehicles and bicycles and may require the use of pistols, long guns, shot guns, chemical spray, impact weapons, knives, and any other tool used as a defensive weapon. 3. Investigate disturbances or criminal violations occurring on university or surrounding property; perform all tasks necessary to restore peace and order or apprehend possible offenders. May require the physical ability to exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Requires the physical fitness level that meets current criminal justice standards. Requires the physical ability to sit for extended periods of time and drive patrol vehicles. May require the ability to run, jump, stand, and walk for long periods of time, and the ability to physically subdue an offender with reasonable force and have reasonable strength to perform necessary lifesaving functions. Task requires a wide field of vision and the visual ability to perceive depth and distinguish colors. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to read, write, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information, and to receive, comprehend and follow oral instructions and information. Requires the mental ability to analyze problem situations and adjust to varying work assignments, use judgment and discretion, and demonstrate appropriate written and verbal communication skills. Task requires use of vehicles and bicycles and may require the use of pistols, long guns, shot guns, chemical spray, impact weapons, knives, and any other tool used as a defensive weapon. 4. Investigate vehicle accidents on university or surrounding property; conduct appropriate investigations, provide necessary emergency care, and assist as necessary. May require the physical ability to exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Requires the physical fitness level that meets current criminal justice standards. Requires the physical ability to sit for extended periods of time and drive patrol vehicles. May require the ability to run, jump, stand, and walk for long periods of time, and the ability to physically subdue a