retion, and demonstrate appropriate written and verbal communication skills. Task may require use of vehicles, bicycles, pistols, long guns, shot guns, chemical spray, impact weapons, knives, and any other tool used as a defensive weapon. 8. Assist members of the community and other law enforcement agencies in an appropriate manner. May require the physical ability to exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Requires the physical fitness level that meets current criminal justice standards. Requires the physical ability to sit for extended periods of time and drive patrol vehicles. Requires the ability to run, jump, stand, and walk for long periods of time, and the ability to physically subdue an offender with reasonable force and have reasonable strength to perform necessary lifesaving functions. Task requires a wide field of vision and the visual ability to perceive depth and distinguish colors. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to read, write, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information, and to receive, comprehend and follow oral instructions and information. Requires the mental ability to analyze problem situations and adjust to varying work assignments, use judgement and discretion, and demonstrate appropriate written and verbal communication skills. Task requires use of vehicles, bicycles, pistols, long guns, shot guns, chemical spray, impact weapons, knives, and any other tool used as a defensive weapon. Task may require use of Automated External Defibrillator and the ability to perform  CPR . 9. Perform community policing initiatives as directed by the department. May require the physical ability to exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Requires the physical fitness level that meets current criminal justice standards. Requires the physical ability to sit for extended periods of time and drive patrol vehicles. Requires the ability to run, jump, stand, and walk for long periods of time, and the ability to physically subdue an offender with reasonable force and have reasonable strength to perform necessary lifesaving functions. Task requires a wide field of vision and the visual ability to perceive depth and distinguish colors. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to read, write, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information, and to receive, comprehend and follow oral instructions and information. Requires the mental ability to analyze problem situations and adjust to varying work assignments, use judgment and discretion, and demonstrate appropriate written and verbal communication skills. Task requires use of vehicles, bicycles, pistols, long guns, shot guns, chemical spray, impact weapons, knives, and any other tool used as a defensive weapon. Task requires use of Automated External Defibrillator and the ability to perform CPR. 10. Prepare and write detailed reports; investigate all accidents, criminal cases, and incidents to provide complete documentation for Ball State; provide necessary information to assist the prosecutor’s office in preparing criminal cases. Task requires the mental ability to read, write reports, keep records, pay attention to detail, testify in court, and comprehend and follow instructions and information. Requires the mental ability to analyze problem situations and adjust to varying work assignments, use judgment and discretion, and demonstrate appropriate written and verbal communication skills. 11. Provide security/escort and transportation for campus cash transactions. Requires the physical ability to sit for extended periods of time, drive patrol vehicles, run, jump, stand, and walk for long periods of time. Task requires a wide field of vision and the visual ability to perceive depth and distinguish colors. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to read, write, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information. Requires the mental ability to analyze problem situations and adjust to varying work assignments, use judgment and discretion, and demonstrate appropriate written and verbal communication skills. Task may require use of vehicles and/or bicycles. 12. Perform other related duties as assigned. May require any of the above-mentioned abilities. Minimum Qualifications: 1. High School Diploma or GED. 2. Must possess and maintain a valid Driver’s License and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. 3. Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty and be able to meet physical fitness standards as defined by the Indiana Law Enforcement Academy. 4. Must pass a written examination and polygraph test pre-offer. 5. Must pass a post offer/pre-employment psychological evaluation, medical, drug and alcohol test. 6. Must pass skills test. 7. Must be at least age 21 at time of hire. 8. Must be a U.S. Citizen in accordance with Indiana code 250IAC 2-3-1. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Associate’s degree or two years of college or equivalent experience in law enforcement or two years of active military service in the U.S. Armed Forces. 2. Bachelor’s degree. 3. Successful completion of the Indiana Law Enforcement Academy basic training course, or completion of an equivalent training program approved by the Indiana Law Enforcement Training Board. 4. Law enforcement experience related to a campus/university environment. How to apply: Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:  Do  not  use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: Resume Optional Document: Cover Letter   detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
