    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-Anthropology_R-03116": {
      "title": "Instructor of Anthropology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of Anthropology Compensation: 3000.00 per class Department: Department of Anthropology and Sociology - Temp Start Date: 01/11/2027 About this opportunity:   The Department of Anthropology and Sociology invites applications for its temporary, part-time Instructor of Anthropology pool. Applicants selected for the pool may be offered assignments to teach one or two undergraduate courses per semester, depending on departmental instructional needs and course availability. These are temporary appointments and are not permanent or tenure-track positions. There is no guarantee of a teaching assignment in any semester, and opportunities for future assignments are dependent on departmental needs. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Applications will be held on file for one year. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: Faculty in the pool may be needed to teach a variety of undergraduate courses, such as Introduction to Cultural Anthropology, Archaeology and Culture, and Introduction to Biological Anthropology, in either online or in-person formats during the fall and spring semesters. Course assignments will vary based on departmental instructional needs and course availability. Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in Anthropology from an accredited institution. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in Anthropology from an accredited institution and demonstrated excellence in teaching anthropology at the postsecondary level. Experience in teaching in-person and online classes. Area of specialization (as evidenced by coursework or teaching experience) congruent with departmental course needs. Commitment to high-quality teaching is essential. How to apply:   Please provide the following: Required Documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Undergraduate Transcripts Optional Documents: Master's Transcripts If you have questions please contact: Robert Phillips rfphillips@bsu.edu 765-285-4845"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Bookkeeper-and-Auditor_R-02945-1": {
      "title": "Bookkeeper and Auditor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Bookkeeper and Auditor Compensation: $15.00 - 16.26 Department: North Dining Start Date: 09/14/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Dining has an opportunity for a Bookkeeper and Auditor position. This opportunity comes with a great benefit package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, University-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more! This is a full-time, on-campus opportunity. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Perform bookkeeping and auditing tasks under firm deadlines, including but not limited to accounts payable, accounts receivable, and typing/routing of food and supply transfers; audit count of reserve money, meal period and daily cashier reports, and sales deposit monies; maintain adequate monies in proper denominations for cashiering function; prepare records for financial reporting, including but not limited to inventory evaluations, submittal of bills for payment, and invoices for payments due and meet requirements for end-of-the-month financial reports; type and send overdue notices; maintain and submit financial records, royalty payments, and reports required by contracted brands vendors; perform general office duties such as office equipment cleaning, answering telephone, communicating messages, requesting supplies, and maintaining files; utilize computer spreadsheet software, copy machine, and calculator. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Audit vendor invoices to BSU purchase orders; reconcile differences with vendors and/or unit management; type accounts payable vouchers and process via BSU Accounting Department for payment; type and process food and supply move orders; meet deadlines. 2. Audit daily cashier check-out sheets and cashier sales deposits; prepare sales deposit reports; submit sales deposits and reports to Bursar, report errors to management; audit and verify reports with POS cash system; prepare sales spreadsheet by concept each day, week, and month, then reconcile the daily sales deposits with the monthly financial reports; meet deadlines. 3. Audit cash POS (Point of Sale cash registers) records for accurate daily report of product movement of each menu item for each branded concept or food station; prepare computer spreadsheets to report product movement, value of sales, and royalties due each vendor; submit royalty authorizations to the Accounting Office for payment; meet deadlines. 4. Scrutinize records and then prepare monthly reports of inventory valuation, purchases, accounts payable, accounts receivable, journal vouchers for transfers, royalty payments, etc; submit to proper office locations; meet deadlines. 5. Collect receipts for pick-up sales, maintain adequate monies in proper denomination for revenue centers and maintain an accurate record of reserve monies and safe shortages; report discrepancies to the General Manager immediately. 6. Provide excellent customer service, including but not limited to interacting with customers, answering the telephone efficiently and courteously for incoming calls; route calls to proper person, taking accurate and thorough messages to provide accurate information and effectively communicating information to management in a timely, friendly, and courteous manner. 7. Audit all purchase orders against requisition lists to ensure orders exist, delivery dates are accurate, and vendor product code numbers are correct; notify management of discrepancies between purchase orders and vendor invoices. 8. Maintain up-to-date price and delivery records for all items purchased; enter corrections and receiving code numbers into computer system; and assist with annual unit fiscal inventory; meet deadlines. 9. Prepare estimated 100 client journal vouchers or invoices for meals, refreshments and services; submit to Student Financial Services for processing within the established business month; audit revenue accounts on the monthly financial statements to verify that client journal vouchers or invoices were correctly posted; audit revenue accounts on a monthly basis to ensure accounts receivables (off-campus and intra-university invoices) are paid; trace unpaid accounts and send overdue notices. 10. Perform other related duties as assigned, including but not limited to; reporting office repair needs, requisitioning office supplies, maintaining storage of department records according to guidelines and cleaning and maintaining office equipment. 11. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. Minimum Qualifications: Up to eighteen months of bookkeeping, auditing, accounting, or related training or education beyond high school or equivalent. One to three years of bookkeeping, auditing, or accounting experience; excellent computer skills in Windows Word, Excel and Outlook. Excellent computer skills in Windows Word, Excel and Outlook. Demonstrated excellence in customer service. Demonstrated ability to work in an environment with frequent interruptions and changes. Preferred Qualifications: Associates degree from an accredited college or university in bookkeeping, auditing, or accounting. Proficiency in the use of computer software: Cbord Menu Management, Excel, Word, Google. Database experience in POS cash handling systems, cash sales reporting and tracking. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: University Dining at 765-285-1967. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Please follow upload instructions to attach all supporting documents.  Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: 1. Resume Optional Document (Recommended for Best Consideration): 2. Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Internal-Audit-Specialist_R-02989": {
      "title": "Internal Audit Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Internal Audit Specialist Compensation: $55,000-$65,000 Department: Internal Auditing & Advisory Srvs About this opportunity: Ball State University welcomes applications for an Internal Audit Specialist. The Internal Audit Specialist reports to the Director of Internal Audit and Advisory Services (Director) or the Director’s designated deputy. The job holder will lead and execute risk-based audit projects with limited supervision from the Director. This is a full-time professional staff position. The expected start date is as soon as possible. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Multiple vacancies may be filled by this posting. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Lead and execute risk-based audit projects with limited supervision of the Director of Internal Audit. Position requires proficiency with the following: understanding the university's operations, strategic goals and imperatives, key business processes, assessing risks, developing audit programs, utilizing data analytics in audits, auditing controls, and providing recommendations that create value to the area under audit; audit report and general writing that is succinct, clear and professional; completing audit workpaper documentation that aligns with the newly introduced Ball State Audit Methodology and Internal Audit Standards. Must cultivate and maintain relationships with manager-level (and below) stakeholders across the campus and educate the stakeholders about governance, risk management, and internal control activities. In charge of coordinating the work of others if assigned to lead a project with other auditors, and following up on the implementation of the agreed management actions (audit recommendations) as assigned.   Duties and Responsibilities: Perform governance, financial, compliance, operational, and technology audit procedures, including identifying and defining issues. Research statutes, State of Indiana and federal regulations, and other internal and external guidelines affecting the area or process under review. Determine risk areas and the objective of the audit. Determine the operational processes and business objectives in place, and create testing programs to assess the operations based on the goals established Review and analyze evidence and document client processes and procedures. Conduct interviews, review information (data, documents, etc.), develop and administer surveys, compose summary memos, and document and maintain working papers. Understand and document complex financial and business processes. Communicate clearly through written and verbal channels to internal audiences in a way to elevate partnership and collaboration. Incorporate data analytics and/or automation in audit procedures to drive efficiencies. Identify, develop, and document audit issues and recommendations using independent judgment concerning areas being reviewed. Maintain minutes/documentation of the opening, process discussions, and closing meetings. Communicate or provide support in communicating the results of audit and consulting projects via written reports and oral presentations to management. Develop and maintain productive client and staff relationships through individual contacts and group meetings. Provide support in identifying and evaluating the University’s risk areas and providing input into the development of the Annual Audit Plan. Pursue professional development opportunities, including external and internal training and professional association memberships, and sharing information gained with co-workers. Represent Internal Audit and Advisory Services on University project teams and at management meetings. Cultivate and maintain relationships with Manager-level and specialist-level stakeholders. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in Business, Accounting, Auditing, Finance, Information Systems, or related discipline. One to three years of internal auditing experience in a University environment, governmental, non-profit, or related industry, and/or other professional experience in higher education. Demonstrated understanding of State of Indiana and Federal laws relating to higher education. Demonstrated solid communication and listening skills and an ability to identify gaps in logic and handle complex communication challenges individually. Ability to communicate effectively to internal audiences on complex results in a way to gain common understanding. Demonstrated ability to identify sensitive issues and proactively facilitate effective communication at various levels in the university to avoid surprises. Strong analytical and critical thinking with proven examples of continuous learning. Teachable and adaptable. Proficient in managing (including changing) priorities and working on multiple projects simultaneously. Ability to work with varied constituents.  Commitment to objectivity, confidentiality, and mental independence.   Preferred Qualifications Professional certification(s) in internal auditing (CIA), public accounting (CPA), Information technology (CISA), and/or fraud examination (CFE) upon date of hire OR must attain one of these certifications within 2 years of hire. Knowledge of the Banner System and other ERPs. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Chifundo Biliwita, Director of Internal Audit and Advisory Services, at the following email address: chifundo.biliwita@bsu.edu Please list three professional references within the online application.   Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume: Please follow the upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Executive-Assistant-to-the-Vice-President_R-03120": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant to the Vice President",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Executive Assistant to the Vice President Compensation: $22.00 - 24.20 Department: VP for Business Affairs/Treasurer Start Date: 10/09/2026 About this opportunity: This opportunity is a high-level administrative role supporting the Vice President for Business Affairs and Treasurer. The position involves managing calendars, coordinating meetings and events, handling correspondence, tracking projects, and supporting financial and personnel processes. It requires strong organization, communication, discretion, attention to detail, and the ability to prioritize competing responsibilities. Overall, this role provides an opportunity to work closely with senior leadership while helping ensure the Business Affairs office operates efficiently and effectively. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Provide and oversee administrative and executive secretarial support services for the Vice President for Business Affairs and Treasurer. Duties & Responsibilities: 1 . Serve as the primary administrative coordinator and communicator for the Vice President of Business Affairs, exercising sound judgment, professionalism, discretion, and confidentiality in all interactions and responsibilities. 2. Maintain the Vice President’s daily calendar; schedule, coordinate, and confirm meetings with university leadership, cabinet members, deans, department heads, faculty, staff, external partners, and other stakeholders. Evaluate meeting requests and prioritize commitments based on urgency and organizational needs. Compose, edit, proofread, and distribute correspondence, reports, memoranda, presentations, and other documents. 3. Prepare agendas, background materials, reports, presentations, and other supporting documentation for meetings. Ensure the Vice President has the appropriate information and materials in advance and track follow-up items and commitments resulting from meetings. Plan and coordinate meetings, retreats, conferences, special events, presentations, and other activities sponsored or supported by the Office of Business Affairs. 4. Monitor the flow of projects, correspondence, requests, and other information through the Office of Business Affairs. Review, organize, and route information to appropriate personnel; assemble related information to facilitate timely decisions and ensure projects and assignments receive appropriate attention. 5. Serve as a central point of contact for the Vice President’s office and collaborate effectively with senior administrators, Business Affairs personnel, other university offices, faculty, staff, students, vendors, government and community representatives, and members of the public. 6. Provide administrative support for financial activities within the Vice President’s area of responsibility, including purchase requisitions, invoices, journal vouchers, payment requests, procurement transactions, foundation payments, travel, review monthly statements and invoices, and other financial documentation. Review materials for completeness and accuracy and route items for appropriate approval. 7. Arrange travel for the Vice President and designated leadership personnel, including travel authorizations, registrations, lodging, transportation, vehicle requests, and expense reimbursements. Ensure travel documentation is complete, accurate, and processed in a timely manner. 8. Assist the Vice President with the coordination and administrative tracking of facilities, space, maintenance, capital, operational, and other business-related initiatives. Gather information, organize documentation, monitor deadlines, and facilitate communication among departments and stakeholders. 9. Maintain tracking systems for projects, action items, deadlines, approvals, and other assignments. Follow up with appropriate personnel as needed to facilitate completion and keep the Vice President informed of outstanding matters. 10. Assist with administrative aspects of recruitment, position postings, position descriptions, onboarding, personnel documentation, employee records, payroll-related documents, personnel action forms, and other employment processes as assigned. Maintain appropriate personnel files and protect confidential employee information. 11. Receive and respond appropriately to telephone calls, correspondence, visitors, and inquiries. Provide general information regarding established university policies and procedures and direct specialized questions to the appropriate personnel while maintaining professionalism and confidentiality. 12. Ensure appropriate office coverage, including use of student staff, and continuity of administrative support. Coordinate with other administrative personnel regarding schedules, absences, workload distribution, and backup coverage. 13. Monitor office supplies, equipment, forms, and other administrative resources; place orders as necessary; maintain organized workspaces and administrative systems; and identify opportunities to improve office efficiency and effectiveness. 14. Identify opportunities to improve administrative processes, information management, communication, and workflow. Learn and utilize new software, electronic forms, financial systems, document-management tools, and other technologies to increase efficiency, accuracy, and productivity. 15. Perform notary services and other specialized administrative functions for the University as authorized and needed. 16. Establish priorities, resolve routine administrative issues, anticipate the needs of the Vice President and the office, and determine appropriate courses of action while recognizing matters requiring escalation or executive attention. Maintain a high level of accuracy and organization when managing calendars, financial transactions, records, correspondence, meetings, deadlines, and confidential information. Establish and maintain effective working relationships across all levels of the University and with external constituents. 17. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned in support of the Vice President, the Office of Business Affairs, and the overall mission and strategic priorities of the University. 18. Maintain regular and predictable attendance and be available during established working hours to ensure continuity of executive and administrative support. Minimum Qualifications: Associate’s degree secretarial science or equivalent. Over three through five years of secretarial or office management experience. Must hold an Indiana Notary License or be able to secure an Indiana Notary License within 90 days. Handle confidential and sensitive financial, personnel, operational, facilities, legal, and institutional information with a high degree of discretion. Maintain confidentiality in communications, records, meetings, and interactions with internal and external constituents. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Knowledge of graphic and spreadsheet software. How to apply: Please apply via the online Ball State University job portal . Please list three professional references within the online application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:  Do  not  use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: Resume ​ ​Optional Document: Cover Letter What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Gymnastics-Coach_R-02608": {
      "title": "Assistant Gymnastics Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Gymnastics Coach Compensation: $41,500 - $43,710 Department: Gymnastics About this opportunity: Ball State University and Ball State Athletics are committed to developing championship-caliber student-athletes who excel in competition, in the classroom, and in the community. The Assistant Gymnastics Coach will join a passionate and collaborative team dedicated to competitive success, student development, and the values that define Cardinal athletics. Recognized as one of Indiana’s top employers, Ball State provides a welcoming campus community, outstanding professional opportunities, competitive benefits packages, and a culture centered on growth, excellence, and Beneficence - the University’s commitment to making a positive difference in the lives of others. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Provide teaching and instruction to student-athletes; perform duties in all areas of the program at the direction of the head coach, athletic director, and/or sport supervisor. Duties and Responsibilities: Provide teaching and instruction to student-athletes. Develop, in conjunction with the head coach, planning of practice sessions and competitive coaching situations. Assess and evaluate talent and recruitment of athletes in to the program, includes contact by telephone and mail, off campus evaluations, and on campus visits. Develop scouting reports and pre-competition evaluations of opponents. Make recommendations in regard to fund raising, promotion and marketing, special projects, clinics and camps. Monitor, in conjunction with the head coach, the academic progress, the conditioning, and the training of the student-athletes. Show commitment to and responsibility for adherence to all rules and regulations of Ball State University, the Mid-American Conference, and the NCAA; pass the NCAA certification examination on an annual basis. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university by date of appointment. One year of collegiate and/or Level 10 coaching experience, and/or collegiate competitive experience. Ability to spot Division I collegiate athletes; possess and maintain a valid driver's license and be insurable under the university's auto fleet policy. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited college or university. Three years of collegiate coaching and/or Level 10 coaching experience. How to apply: Please apply via the online Ball State University job portal . Please submit three professional references at the time of application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:  Do  not  use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: Resume Optional Document: Cover Letter   detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Instructors-of-Music--Academic-_R-02363": {
      "title": "Instructors of Music (Academic)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructors of Music (Academic) Compensation: $500 - $9,000 Department: School of Music - Temp Start Date: 08/17/2026 About this opportunity:   The School of Music at Ball State University invites applications for ongoing part-time semester instructor appointments to teach coursework in an on-campus environment. Our faculty are expected to be innovative, adaptive, engaging teachers across modalities; producers of impactful creative and/or scholarly work; leaders in meaningful service activities to multiple communities. We seek faculty members who are strategic thinkers, engaging our dynamic communities. We are committed to student and faculty success, impact, and access. We inspire each other to be critical thinkers and responsible citizens, so that we can pursue fulfilling careers and meaningful lives. Ball State University lives the values of Beneficence. We invite you to be part of our community. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: This is a part time semester instructor position in an on campus environment. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Primary assignment will initially include teaching coursework in music education, music history, music theory/composition, or music technology. Other duties as assigned by the Director of the School of Music. Minimum Qualifications: Completed master’s degree and a documented history of professional activity in the area of assignment. Demonstrated ability to recruit and retain quality students on the collegiate level, exceptional creative/scholarly background. How to apply:   IMPORTANT: To ensure accurate processing of your application, do not rely on a resume upload to populate the job experience section. All work history must be entered directly into the application fields. Required Documents 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae (Do Not use the \"Autofill\" resume feature.) Optional Documents 1. Master's Transcripts 2. Doctorate Transcripts Search Committee Chair Name and Contact Information: Dr. Franklin Larey, Director School of Music, music@bsu.edu Applications will be accepted through August 12, 2026, at 12:01 AM. The option to upload transcripts is available. Original, official transcripts showing the highest related degree earned is required at the time of hire (even if obtained at BSU). Degree verification will be conducted."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-Music--Applied-_R-01872": {
      "title": "Instructor of Music (Applied)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of Music (Applied) Compensation: $500 - $9,000 Department: School of Music - Temp Start Date: 08/17/2026 About this opportunity:   The School of Music at Ball State University invites applications for ongoing part-time semester faculty appointments to teach applied music coursework in an on-campus environment. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Job Description: The primary assignment will initially include teaching applied lessons, coaching chamber music, or conducting ensembles, along with other duties as assigned by the Director of the School of Music. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree from an accredited college or university and a documented history of professional activity in the area of assignment. Demonstrated ability to recruit and retain quality students on the collegiate level, exceptional creative/scholarly background. How to apply:   Required Documents: 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae (Do Not use the \"Autofill\" resume feature) Optional Documents: 1. Master's Transcripts 2. Doctorate Transcripts For inquiries regarding these opportunities, please contact: Dr. Franklin Larey, Director School of Music, music@bsu.edu Applications will be accepted through June 20, 2026, at 12:01 AM."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/University-Architect_R-02855": {
      "title": "University Architect",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: University Architect Compensation: $130,000 - $140,000 Department: FPM Administration About this opportunity: Ball State University Facilities Planning and Management has an opportunity to work on the beautiful campus. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefits package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, university-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more. The ideal candidate will be flexible, and will possess great service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on campus opportunity. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: The University Architect serves as Ball State University's primary steward for campus planning, architectural direction, design standards, and the long-term development of the physical campus. This position provides leadership and oversight for architectural and engineering design efforts across University projects, ensuring that scopes, design concepts, consultant work products, design milestones, and final design solutions align with the Campus Master Plan, University standards, operational needs, budget expectations, sustainability goals, accessibility requirements, and the overall student and campus experience. This position works in close partnership with project managers, Engineering, Construction, Operations, Building Services, campus clients, University leadership, and outside design professionals.                   The University Architect will also advise on the appropriate architectural and engineering design contract structure for each project, including the use and modification of AIA based templates and Ball State contract templates as necessary to protect the owner, clarify scope, monitor changes, manage amendments, and support consistent design contract administration. Duties & Responsibilities 1.  Serve as the University's lead architectural advisor and design steward for campus buildings, interiors, landscapes, open spaces, public realm improvements, and other physical campus assets. 2.  Support and advance the implementation of the Campus Master Plan by aligning project planning, building improvements, site development, space needs, and design decisions with the University's long term physical planning goals. 3.  Provide architectural and engineering design oversight for university projects in partnership with assigned project managers. 4.  Work with project managers to ensure that external architects, engineers, planners, and design consultants understand the University's expectations, standards, operational requirements, campus context, project goals, and owner interests. 5.  Participate in preliminary scope development for all applicable projects, including client discussions, feasibility review, project intent, conceptual options, planning level budgets, design direction, and identification of required architectural and engineering support. 6.  Support project managers during the transition from preliminary scope development to consultant led design and project execution. 7.  Review design work at key project milestones, including concept development, schematic design, design development, construction documents, and other major review points as appropriate. 8.  Provide high level review of architectural and engineering design packages to confirm alignment with approved scope, campus standards, maintainability, accessibility, sustainability, budget expectations, owner requirements, and long-term operational needs. 11.  Advise project managers and University leadership on the appropriate architectural and engineering design contract structure for specific projects, including scope of services, milestone deliverables, consultant responsibilities, amendment needs, and owner protection considerations. 12.  Review, recommend, and coordinate modifications to AIA based agreement templates and Ball State contract templates as necessary to protect the University as owner, clarify design scope, monitor changes, manage amendments, and support consistent administration of design contracts. 13.  Develop, maintain, interpret, and promote University design standards, architectural guidelines, space standards, finish standards, furniture standards, signage standards, and related planning and design expectations. 15.  Review renovation, renewal, new construction, infrastructure, and site improvement concepts for consistency with campus character, building context, operational practicality, code awareness, accessibility, sustainability, life cycle cost, and owner stewardship considerations. 16.  Provide design leadership on projects that require strong coordination between architectural, engineering, operational, custodial, maintenance, technology, safety, accessibility, procurement, contract, and client needs. 18.  Advise campus clients and University leadership on project feasibility, planning options, design implications, space impacts, phasing considerations, cost drivers, delivery options, contract implications, and long-term facility impacts. 19.  Partner with Engineering and Operations to ensure that design decisions account for building systems, maintainability, staffing impacts, energy use, utility infrastructure, service access, operational continuity, and future renewal needs. 20.  Partner with Construction and project management staff to ensure that design intent, approved scope, contract expectations, and University standards are carried through design, bidding, construction, occupancy, and closeout. 21.  Support space planning and utilization efforts, including evaluation of space requests, development of options, review of existing conditions, and recommendations that support academic, administrative, student service, and operational needs. 22.  Support capital planning and asset renewal planning by helping identify facility needs, design priorities, scope considerations, planning level budgets, and alignment with the Campus Master Plan. 23.  Represent Facilities Planning and Management in meetings with campus clients, consultants, contractors, public agencies, University leadership, and other stakeholders. 24.  Promote a planning and design process that is collaborative, transparent, service oriented, fiscally responsible, legally aware, contractually disciplined, and aligned with the mission of the University. 25.  Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications 1.  Bachelor's degree in Architecture from an accredited program. 2.  Licensed architect in any United States jurisdiction, with the ability to obtain Indiana architectural registration within twelve months of hire. 3.  At least ten years of progressively responsible experience in architecture, facility planning, campus planning, design management, project programming, design contract support, or related work. 4.  Demonstrated experience developing or reviewing project scopes, feasibility studies, design concepts, design documents, planning studies, architectural standards, or consultant scopes of service. 5.  Demonstrated experience working with architects, engineers, contractors, consultants, project managers, internal clients, operational stakeholders, and contract or procurement partners. 6.  Knowledge of building codes, accessibility requirements, construction documents, project delivery processes, design standards, consultant agreements, scope amendments, and construction administration. 7.  Ability to review architectural and engineering design work and provide clear, practical, and constructive direction. 8.  Ability to communicate effectively with technical and non-technical audiences. 9.  Ability to manage competing priorities, build consensus, exercise sound judgment, and provide recommendations in a complex institutional environment. Preferred Qualifications 1.  Master's degree in Architecture, Campus Planning, Urban Planning, Historic Preservation, Construction Management, Real Estate, Public Administration, Business Administration, or a related field. 2. Ten or more years of progressive experience in higher education, public sector, civic, cultural, healthcare, research, or other complex institutional environments. 3.  Experience working in an owner representative environment. 4.  Experience with campus master planning, space planning, capital planning, design guidelines, accessibility planning, historic campus stewardship, public realm planning, or design contract administration. 5.  Experience developing or managing pools of on call architects, engineers, planners, interior designers, landscape architects, or design consultants. 6.  Experience reviewing or modifying AIA based design agreement templates, consultant scopes of service, contract amendments, or owner focused design contract provisions. 7.  Experience supervising or leading professional staff in architecture, planning, interior design, space management, or related disciplines. 8.  Experience with AutoCAD, Revit, BIM, Bluebeam, GIS, space management systems, project management systems, or other facilities related platforms. 9.  LEED AP, WELL, Fitwel, NCARB certification, AICP, or other relevant professional credential. 10.  Experience integrating sustainability, accessibility, life cycle cost, maintainability, contractual discipline, and operational continuity into planning and design decisions. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Melissa Wormer, Director of Facilities Management, smwormer@bsu.edu   or 765-285-1630. Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume. Cover Letter (Optional) Resume (Required) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Temporary-Performance-Nutrition-Fellowship_R-02083": {
      "title": "Temporary Performance Nutrition Fellowship",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Temporary Performance Nutrition Fellowship Compensation: $33.33 Department: Intercollegiate Athletics Ops - Temp Start Date: 09/15/2026 About this opportunity:   Ball State University Athletics is seeking applications for Championship Performance Nutrition Fellow.  The Nutrition Fellow will work under the supervision of the Director of Performance Nutrition in conjunction with the Senior Associate Athletic Director for Championship Performance. This is an on-campus position with flexible hours as determined by the department need and Director of Performance Nutrition.  The position requires the Fellow to work 10-12 hours per week for approximately 30 weeks, running September 2026 – May 2027, following the Ball State academic calendar. The position includes a stipend of $10,000 across the 10-months, and is a non-benefit eligible position. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Essential Functions Assist with food service management and daily operations including but not limited to inventory, product ordering, fueling station aesthetics and education. Develop educational materials & resources, including social media content. Develop and deliver nutrition education presentations, demonstrations, or events related to performance to assigned teams. Attend team workouts, practices, and games as needed to provide education and fuel to enhance performance. Assist with travel nutrition needs for assigned teams – performance menus, pre/post-game fuel, post-game meals, recovery strategies, and snack bags. Assist with management, oversight, and mentorship of student volunteers/interns. Minimum Requirements Bachelor’s degree in nutrition   Completion of an undergraduate sport nutrition course Skill in the use of personal computer and related software applications Desire to pursue a career within intercollegiate athletics Strong ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing Strong ability to use independent judgement and to manage and impart information Successful competition of a background check Understanding and adherence to NCAA guidelines Preferred Requirements Master’s Degree in Nutrition or Exercise Physiology Registered Dietitian Completion of a graduate level sport nutrition course. How to apply:   Interested applicants must apply online and include a current CV/Resume, and 3 professional references with their current contact information and job titles in their application materials. The option to include a cover letter is available. For more information reach out to Dr. Kathie Beals, Director of Performance Nutrition, kathiebeals@yahoo.com,  or Dr. Lindsey Blom, Senior Associate AD of Championship Performance, lcblom@bsu.edu"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Academic-Advisor_R-02833": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Academic Advisor Compensation: $43,999 - $45,000 Department: Vc Prov Stu Success & Dean Unv Coll_H About this opportunity: Academic Advisors within University College at Ball State University strive to empower and inspire students to develop a meaningful academic experience using the array of high-quality opportunities and educational tools provided by the university to become impactful leaders in their academic field and community. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Academic Advisors within University College at Ball State University strive to empower and inspire students to develop a meaningful academic experience using the array of high-quality opportunities and educational tools provided by the university to become impactful leaders in their academic field and community. Utilizing a student-centered approach, academic advisors are dedicated to teaching students how to successfully access academic information and connect to crucial resources as well as equipping them with the skills necessary to develop a high-quality educational experience and achieve timely graduation. This position will provide comprehensive and proactive academic advising, promote student success strategies, and guide students in understanding their degree requirements, academic policies, university procedures, and the university resources available to make informed decisions regarding their degree program. Duties and Responsibilities: Provide proactive advising to an assigned caseload of approximately 300 students to provide information and guidance on academic-related issues such as course planning and registration, degree requirements, and academic progress. Provide support to students by creating and maintaining personalized four-year degree plans as mandated by the State of Indiana; train students to interpret the Stellic degree audit and use Self-Service Banner (SSB). Promote strategies for success with students including time management, study tips, and participation in tutoring and supplemental instruction sessions; conduct proactive/intrusive outreach to high support students; provide additional intervention with assigned students in the process of academic warning. Participate in appropriate admissions and orientation events; assist new transfer students and collaborate with academic departments as necessary. Participate in unit-specific and campus-wide retention and student success initiatives. Assist students in exploring career/major options and the use of related campus services; assist students in the selection of alternative and/or complementary major/minor programs. Maintain up-to-date knowledge of university academic programs, requirements, policies, and procedures as outlined in academic postings, the Undergraduate Catalog, the Student Success Handbook, and other resources. Create reports related to student advisee caseloads as directed by academic advising leadership. Assist students in understanding the philosophical purpose and requirements of the University Core Curriculum (UCC). Communicate with academic departments regarding curriculum and advising services as appropriate. Serve as a referral agent to other university resources and services. Represent Academic Advising through service on university committees and participation in campus events; participate in professional development activities. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university by date of employment Experience in academic advising, student services, higher education, counseling, or related field Ability to work with faculty, administration, and undergraduate students Ability to work in a collaborative environment and work independently Sensitivity to the needs of the student population Interpersonal/human relations skills Ability to encourage and empower students to make their own decisions Ability to act as an advocate for both the student and the university Ability to identify students' needs for support services in order to make appropriate referrals Ability to maintain confidentiality Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited college or university by date of employment. Academic advising or student affairs experience. Familiarity with Ball State curriculum. Experience with Banner, Stellic, and EAB Navigate. How to apply: For Inquiries, please contact:  advising@bsu.edu The following documents are required in this application: 1. Cover letter 2. Resume (Do not use the Autofill Resume feature.) Applications must be received before 12:01 AM on September 10, 2026.  What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Director-of-Biomedical-Programs_R-02975": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Biomedical Programs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Director of Biomedical Programs Compensation: $57,000 - $60,000 Department: Biology About this opportunity: The Department of Biology at Ball State University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Director of the Biomedical Sciences Program. This is a full-time, in-person, 12-month professional position. The Department of Biology is one of the largest and most academically active units within the College of Sciences and Humanities. Building on a long record of excellence in teaching, research, and service, the department provides rigorous, hands-on programs that prepare students for success in the biological and biomedical sciences. Students in the biomedical sciences constitute about 40% of the nearly 850+ majors in the Biology Department. Career readiness, mentoring, and advising are all key elements of our students’ journey. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: The primary responsibility for this position is to assist with implementing the Biomedical Sciences program. This includes guiding and managing the program as well as mentoring and advising undergraduates in the program and performing other duties as assigned by the Department Chairperson. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach and assist in the career readiness courses in career readiness courses. Advise students on academics and professional school application preparedness. Develop and deliver workshops, guest speakers, and other professional development opportunities in line with the focus of student programs. Coordinate with the undergraduate curriculum coordinator on program changes and requirements. Participate in recruitment and retention events (may include some evenings and weekends). Support the Director with data gathering, analysis, and report generation. Stay up to date with trends and changes in professional schools and pre-health professions advising via trainings, workshops, and webinars. Perform additional related duties as assigned by the Department Chairperson. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in Biology, biomedical sciences, or a related field from an accredited institution by date of appointment. At least one year of managerial experience in the biomedical or related field. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Biology, biomedical sciences, or a related field from an accredited institution. Experience teaching or advising at the university level. Demonstrated knowledge of and experience working with diverse learners. Familiarity with the application processes for health professions programs and schools. Experience partnering with biomedical agencies. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Dr. Tim Carter at tccarter@bsu.edu. Please follow the upload instructions to attach all of the required documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume. Cover letter Resume or CV Applications must be received before 12:01 AM on September 24, 2026. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Technology-Advisor_R-03072": {
      "title": "Technology Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Technology Advisor Compensation: $50,000 - $60,000 Department: Unified Technology Support_A About this opportunity: Join Information Technology at Ball State University as a Technology Advisor. We are seeking an exceptional communicator and customer service professional with deep expertise in desktop and mobile computing technology. In this role, you will collaborate on campus projects and initiatives to research, propose, and procure technology solutions aligned with strategic university goals. You will also coordinate day-to-day vendor relationships and help guide the evolution of technology at Ball State. This is a great opportunity to help shape the future of technology provided by Ball State University. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Serve as an integral team member who assists with the coordination and procurement of technology for campus initiatives.  Research and propose technology solutions to match the needs of campus partners and associated projects. Serve as the vendor relationship coordinator for Information Technology (IT) and act as the day-to-day point of contact for IT vendors. Collaborate with IT leadership, technical teams, campus partners, budget personnel, and external vendors on technology initiatives and projects. Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Coordinate the overall annual College Technology Plans for all Academic colleges. This may include communicating directly with Deans, Associate Deans, and support staff; Ensure requested technology meets University standards and recommend alternatives as needed; Work with Technology vendors to assure correct and best-priced equipment. 2. Serve as a technology advisor in making recommendations to campus departments on the best technology to meet their needs. Maintain up-to-date knowledge of computer technology. 3. Work with Technology Helpdesk and Desktop Support units, collaborating on orders, scheduling, and installation timelines of new equipment for all campus partners. Communicate directly with partners to set and manage expectations on anticipated timelines. 4. Coordinate with technology vendors and suppliers in support of assigned IT initiatives, procurement activities, and projects. Serve as a point of contact for specific vendor engagements, product inquiries, implementations, and purchasing activities within the scope of assigned responsibilities. Facilitate consistent communication between vendors, IT subject matter experts, IT leadership, and campus stakeholders to support project timelines, deliverables, pricing, and technical requirements.  5. Contact technology vendors for product information, price quotes, availability of items, and order requirements or restrictions. Work with vendors and negotiate when possible to obtain the best overall pricing. Work with vendors to ensure IT Security has the needed Security documentation such as ISO 27001 and/or SOC type 2 reports. Establish and maintain relationships with external vendors to coordinate progress and escalate vendor issues as needed. 6. Work with IT leadership on all technology planning, allocations and budgets ensuring accurate allocations and yearly budgeted amounts are accurately maintained. Work with the vendors and coordinate any contracts with the IT leadership. 7. Collaborate and support IT leadership on projects and strategic initiatives, including the IT Software Review process and other projects as needed. Attend and facilitate meetings, and communicate objectives effectively to team members and partners. 8. Onboard new technology vendors as needed by coordinating required information and documentation. 9. Collaborate on periodic vendor reviews, which may involve scheduling, reviewing proposals, meeting coordination, proposal reviews, competitor identification, vendor research, requesting public records from other universities, organizing, and serving as the point of contact for vendor engagements. 10. Coordinate Request for Proposals (RFP) and Request for Quotes (RFQ) as needed for technology projects. Provide essential documentation and consistent communication as needed to support these processes. 11. Provide timely communication and updates on projects, initiatives, and activities to IT leadership via their preferred means of communication (i.e. ticketing system, email, verbal etc..) 12. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university by date of appointment. Or, in lieu of a Bachelor's degree: 2. Associate's degree plus an additional combination of education or experience in Information Technology equivalent to two years. Or 3. High school diploma or GED plus an additional combination of education or experience in Information Technology equivalent to four years.   At least two years of experience working in a technology procurement, vendor relations, project management, technology support role, or related field.   Excellent oral and written communication skills; exceptional customer service skills; strong analytical and problem-solving skills; strong organizational skills.   Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in computer technology, information systems, computer science, communication, or related area.   Additional years of technology support, project management, and vendor relations experience.   How to apply: Jerry Pierce at rjpierce@bsu.edu Please list three professional references within the online application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Please follow the upload instructions to attach the required supporting document listed below. Required Document: Resume Optional Document: Cover Letter What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Director--Psychoeducational-Diagnostic-and-Intervention-Clinic--PDIC-_R-03012": {
      "title": "Director, Psychoeducational Diagnostic and Intervention Clinic (PDIC)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Director, Psychoeducational Diagnostic and Intervention Clinic (PDIC) Compensation: $80,000-$85,000 Department: TC Deans Office_C About this opportunity: The Psychoeducational Diagnostic and Intervention Clinic (PDIC) is a university-based training and service clinic housed within Teachers College at Ball State University. The clinic provides comprehensive psychoeducational, psychological, developmental, behavioral, and diagnostic assessment services for children, adolescents, adults, families, schools, and community agencies. The PDIC serves as a critical training site for graduate students in School Psychology and related disciplines while providing high-quality, evidence-based services to individuals throughout East Central Indiana and beyond. The clinic supports Ball State University’s commitment to community engagement, experiential learning, and interdisciplinary collaboration by offering assessment, consultation, and intervention services that address academic, behavioral, social-emotional, developmental, and learning needs. Through close partnerships with schools, healthcare providers, families, and community organizations, PDIC contributes to improved educational and behavioral outcomes while preparing future practitioners. PDIC is part of Ball State University’s Interprofessional Community Clinics (ICCs), a collaborative network of clinical and training programs that provide integrated services across disciplines. The ICCs include programs in counseling, audiology, speech-language pathology, autism services, primary care, and other health and human service professions. Through its participation in the ICCs, PDIC contributes to an interprofessional model of care that emphasizes coordinated service delivery, collaborative training, shared operational infrastructure, and improved outcomes for individuals and families across the lifespan. The Director of the Psychoeducational Diagnostic and Intervention Clinic (PDIC) is a 12-month professional staff position responsible for providing strategic, operational, and clinical leadership for the clinic. The position requires a balance of clinical leadership, student supervision, community engagement, operational oversight, and strategic planning to ensure the continued growth, effectiveness, and sustainability of the clinic. Responsibilities include teaching, supervision, clinical work, and clinic administrator oversight - and will ensure the delivery of high-quality assessment and intervention services while supporting the educational and training missions of Teachers College and the Department of Educational Psychology. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function The Director of the Psychoeducational Diagnostic and Intervention Clinic (PDIC) is responsible for providing strategic, operational, and clinical leadership for the clinic. The Director will ensure the delivery of high-quality assessment and intervention services while supporting the educational and training missions of Teachers College and the Department of Educational Psychology. The Director reports to the Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs and Strategic Initiatives in Teachers College and works closely with School Psychology core faculty to support graduate training, accreditation requirements, student supervision, and program development. The Director also collaborates regularly with the directors and leadership team of the Interprofessional Community Clinics to advance interdisciplinary service delivery, shared initiatives, and community partnerships. The position requires a balance of clinical leadership, student supervision, community engagement, operational oversight, and strategic planning to ensure the continued growth, effectiveness, and sustainability of the clinic. The clinic director’s responsibilities will include teaching, supervision, clinical work, and clinic administrator oversight. Duties / Responsibilities 1. Clinical Leadership and Service Delivery Provide leadership for the delivery of high-quality psychoeducational, psychological, behavioral, and related clinical services. Maintain clinical standards consistent with ethical, legal, accreditation, and university requirements (i.e., APTC). Conduct psychological, psychoeducational, developmental, and behavioral assessments as needed. Support the development and expansion of assessment and intervention services responsive to community needs. Ensure appropriate documentation, risk management, and quality assurance practices. Collaborator with the School Psychology EdS and PhD program in the Department of Educational Psychology. 2. Student Training and Supervision Supervise graduate student engaged in clinic-based practice, internships, and training experiences. Provide individual and group supervision in assessment, intervention, consultation, professional writing, and ethical practice. Collaborate with School Psychology faculty to support student learning outcomes, accreditation requirements, and professional competencies. Participate in the development and evaluation of clinical training experiences and student performance. 3. Clinic Administration and Operations Oversee day-to-day clinic operations, including scheduling processes, assessment materials, technology systems, record management, and workflow procedures. Collaborate with ICC administrative and operational personnel to support efficient clinic functioning. Monitor clinic utilization, financial performance, service outcomes, referral patterns, and client satisfaction. Develop and implement policies and procedures that promote operational effectiveness and service quality. Ensure compliance with HIPAA, FERPA, university policies, professional standards, and state regulations. 4. Interprofessional Community Clinic Collaboration Serve as the PDIC representative within the Interprofessional Community Clinics. Collaborate with ICC directors and leadership to support interdisciplinary service delivery and coordinated care models. Develop referral pathways and collaborative programming across clinic units. Participate in ICC planning, assessment, strategic initiatives, and quality improvement efforts. Support interprofessional education and training opportunities for students across disciplines. 5. Community Engagement and Strategic Development Cultivate and maintain partnerships with schools, healthcare providers, community agencies, and other stakeholders. Promote awareness of clinic services through outreach, presentations, and professional engagement activities. Contribute to strategic planning efforts that support clinic growth and sustainability. Support grant development, philanthropic initiatives, and external funding opportunities. Represent PDIC, Teachers College, the ICCs, and Ball State University in professional and community settings. 6. Additional Responsibilities Participate in departmental, college, and university initiatives as appropriate. Contribute to continuous improvement efforts that support student success, community engagement, and clinical excellence. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Doctoral degree in School Psychology, Clinical Psychology, Counseling Psychology, or a related psychology discipline from an accredited institution. Licensed Psychologist in the State of Indiana as a Health Service Provider in Psychology (HSPP), or eligibility for Indiana licensure at the time of appointment. Experience conducting psychoeducational, psychological, and behavioral assessments across various populations. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with key stakeholders. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in School Psychology from a NASP or APA-accredited program Minimum of two years of professional experience providing psychological assessment and intervention services beyond doctoral internship or postdoctoral training. Demonstrated experience supervising graduate students, trainees, or clinical staff. Indiana licensure or eligibility as a School Psychologist. Experience working within university-based training clinics. Experience collaborating with K–12 schools and educational agencies. Experience with interdisciplinary or integrated healthcare service delivery models. Experience with clinic administration, budgeting, strategic planning, quality improvement, and program development. Experience pursuing or managing grants, contracts, or external partnerships. Strong organizational, communication, and leadership skills. How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact: Shannon Dieringer ( sdieringer@bsu.edu ) Please follow upload instructions for attaching all required supporting application documents listed below. Only complete applications submitted through Workday, including the required documents, will be considered. REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS: A cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the position A current résumé - Please do not use the Autofill feature for resume Within the application, please provide contact information for three professional references The option to upload your transcript is available but is not required at the time of application. Original, official transcripts from the issuing institution reflecting the highest related earned degree is required at the time of hire (even if your degree is obtained at Ball State University). The application deadline is: September 12, 2026, 12:01 a.m. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Psychologist-and-Director-of-the-Center-for-Autism-Spectrum-Disorders_R-03018": {
      "title": "Psychologist and Director of the Center for Autism Spectrum Disorders",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Psychologist and Director of the Center for Autism Spectrum Disorders Compensation: $80,000-$85,000 Department: TC Deans Office_C About this opportunity: The Center for Autism Spectrum Disorders (CASD) strives to be a comprehensive training and research hub dedicated to advancing knowledge and practice in autism spectrum disorder (ASD). CASD provides Ball State University students with hands-on training in autism diagnostic evaluation, evidence-based intervention strategies, and collaborative consultation practices. The CASD offers a wide range of services and resources, including diagnostic evaluation, family-centered support, and professional development opportunities. The core component of the CASD is to conduct innovative, interdisciplinary research that informs best practices in assessment, intervention, and service delivery for individuals with ASD across the lifespan. The mission of the CASD is threefold: (a) to provide training opportunities for undergraduate and graduate students to learn and implement autism diagnostic evaluation and intervention services; (b) to provide services and resources in partnership with the community, including intervention, consultation, and individual and group student-centered support and services; and (c) to conduct innovative research to inform practice. The CASD Director is a licensed psychologist with a PsyD or PhD in psychology or related field who has the endorsement as an HSPP and will provide leadership and oversight for the Center for Autism Spectrum Disorder, supervise students in clinical training activities, teach one course within the area of clinical expertise for the Department of Special Education, and conduct psychological evaluations for autism referrals. This is a 12-month position that can provide continuity of services throughout the calendar year. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Provide leadership and oversight for the Center for Autism Spectrum Disorder, supervise students in clinical training activities, teach one course within the area of clinical expertise for the Department of Special Education, and conduct psychological evaluations for autism referrals. Duties / Responsibilities: 1. Program Administration Assist with oversight and coordination of clinic operations, programming, and service delivery. Contribute to outreach, community partnerships, and campus initiatives that enhance awareness and access to services. Support student training, supervision coordination, and program development initiatives for students in the department of special education, department of educational psychology, and/or closely related fields. Maintain compliance with university, ethical, and licensure standards, including documentation, confidentiality, and billing procedures. Represent the CASD, Teachers College, the ICCs, and Ball State University in professional and community settings. 2. Clinical Services & Assessment Conduct psychological assessments for community clients and university students, including clinical interviews, behavioral observations, and standardized testing. Administer, score, interpret, and communicate results of cognitive, personality, and neurodevelopmental assessments related to autism spectrum disorder (ASD) and other mental health concerns. Provide evidence-based individual and group therapy for students with ASD and co-occurring mental health conditions. Develop individualized support plans and provide psychoeducation, consultation, and family support as appropriate. 3. Interprofessional Community Clinic Collaboration Serve as the CASD representative within the Interprofessional Community Clinics. Collaborate with ICC directors and leadership to support interdisciplinary service delivery and coordinated care models. Develop referral pathways and collaborative programming across clinic units. Participate in ICC planning, assessment, strategic initiatives, and quality improvement efforts. Support interprofessional education and training opportunities for students across disciplines. 4. Teaching and Supervision Supervise graduate assistants and practicum students. Teach one class per semester in the Department of Special Education. 5. Student Support Support autistic students in navigating academic, social, and daily challenges within the university setting. Collaborate with disability services, student success programs, faculty, and community providers to coordinate care and promote inclusion for neurodiverse students. Provide consultation and training to faculty and staff regarding best practices for supporting students with ASD. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in clinical or school psychology from an accredited university. Licensed Psychologist in the State of Indiana as a Health Service Provider in Psychology (HSPP), or eligibility for Indiana licensure at the time of appointment. Expertise in the diagnosis and treatment of autism spectrum disorder. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with key stakeholders. Strong organizational, communication, and leadership skills. Preferred Qualifications: Three years post-licensure experience. Completion of a post-doctoral fellowship in autism spectrum disorders. Experience working with autistic adults. Experience teaching undergraduate and graduate students. Board Certified Behavior Analyst Certification. Experience with interdisciplinary or integrated healthcare service delivery models. Experience with clinic administration, budgeting, strategic planning, quality improvement, and program development. Experience pursuing or managing grants, contracts, or external partnerships. How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact: Shannon Dieringer ( sdieringer@bsu.edu ) Please follow upload instructions for attaching all required supporting application documents listed below. Only complete applications submitted through Workday, including the required documents, will be considered. REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS: A cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the position A current résumé - Please do not use the Autofill feature for resume Within the application, please provide contact information for three professional references The option to upload your transcript is available but is not required at the time of application. Original, official transcripts from the issuing institution reflecting the highest related earned degree is required at the time of hire (even if your degree is obtained at Ball State University). The application deadline is: September 12, 2026 12:01 a.m. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Lecturer-Assistant-Teaching-Professor-of-Entrepreneurship_R-03020-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor of Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor of Entrepreneurship Compensation: $60,000 - $90,000 Department: Management Start Date: 01/01/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of Management in the Miller College of Business at Ball State University welcomes applications for a full-time, 10-month contract position with a joining date of January 2027 or August 2027, based on the availability of the candidate and needs of the department. This contract position is renewable based upon the performance of the employee, teaching needs of the department, and budget. Candidates should have the ability to be physically present on Ball State campus multiple days per week and should be prepared to teach both face-to-face and online courses. Student needs will determine the final count of in-person vs online courses. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Position Function: Primary responsibilities include teaching courses in the field of entrepreneurship and/or other areas of management (e.g., leadership, human resource management, international business, organizational behavior). Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching: Anticipated assignments include teaching four classes (12 credits) per semester in the field of entrepreneurship and/or other areas of management (e.g., leadership, human resource management, international business, organizational behavior). Service: Performing service and outreach activities for Ball State University and the community. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in business or related field from an accredited institution. Previous teaching experience at the undergraduate collegiate level.     Preferred Qualifications: Master’s or doctoral degree in business or related field from an AACSB-accredited institution. Significant teaching experience in entrepreneurship at an AACSB-accredited institution. Proven record of service and outreach in the field of entrepreneurship. Required Certifications/Licensures: How to apply: For inquiries about this position, please contact: Dr. Abhishek Srivastava, abhishek.srivastava@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions and attach all required supporting application documents listed below. Only applications submitted through Workday, which include all required documents listed below, will be considered. Required Application Documents: Curriculum Vitae *Please do not use the Autofill feature for resume/vitae Letter of application Teaching Statement When prompted, please provide name and contact information for (3) references within the application Optional Documents: Transcripts may be uploaded at the time of application, however, an official transcript must be received by the issuing institution at the time of employment. Application Deadline: This position will remain open until filled with the consideration date of September 30, 2026. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Marketing_R-02895-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Marketing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Marketing Compensation: $132,000-$137,000 Department: Marketing Start Date: 08/01/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of Marketing in the Miller College of Business at Ball State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Marketing position beginning August 2027. We are a collaborative, student-centered, industry-connected, experientially driven, and forward-looking department committed to preparing students for successful careers in a rapidly changing marketing profession. The successful candidate will join the department at an exciting point in its development. We are strengthening our curriculum, expanding applied learning and industry engagement, and creating more intentional connections across the student experience. The candidate will contribute their own expertise and ideas while working with others to help shape what comes next. We value faculty interested in connecting classroom learning with meaningful applied and immersive experiences that help students develop the knowledge, skills, judgment, and professional readiness needed to succeed. We are seeking a candidate who is excited to contribute through excellent teaching, meaningful scholarship, collaborative engagement, and a genuine investment in the continued growth of our students, programs, and department. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to helping students navigate emerging developments in marketing, including evolving technologies, digital platforms, data-informed decision making, and other innovations shaping the profession. Candidates with an interest and ability to teach undergraduate and/or graduate marketing courses, particularly in one or more of the following areas are strongly encouraged to apply: digital marketing, marketing research, consumer behavior, and marketing analytics. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Position Function Primary responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and/or graduate marketing courses, maintaining an active program of scholarly research, and contributing to the continued success of the Department of Marketing through meaningful service, student engagement, and collaboration with colleagues. Duties and Responsibilities Teaching: Teach 9 semester credit hours of undergraduate and/or graduate marketing courses, with assignments based on departmental needs and the faculty member's expertise. Deliver high-quality instruction in face-to-face and online environments. Develop engaging learning experiences that connect theory and practice through applied, immersive, and industry-engaged learning opportunities, when appropriate. Research: Maintain an active and productive program of scholarly research that demonstrates the potential for sustained scholarly achievement consistent with departmental, college, and AACSB expectations for tenure and promotion. Disseminate research through quality peer-reviewed publications, academic conferences, and other appropriate scholarly outlets. Contribute to a collaborative research culture through scholarly engagement, interdisciplinary collaboration, and when appropriate, the involvement and mentorship of students in research activities. Service: Contribute meaningful service to the department, college, university, profession, and broader community. Contribute to departmental initiatives that advance student success, curriculum innovation, industry engagement, and the department’s shared priorities. Collaborate with colleagues, students, alumni, and external partners to strengthen the department and enhance the student experience. Minimum Qualifications Education: Ph.D. or D.B.A. in Marketing or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited institution. Candidates with ABD will be considered and must demonstrate satisfactory progress toward completion of the doctoral degree consistent with university policy. Experience: Evidence of, or demonstrated potential for, high-quality scholarly research. Evidence of, or demonstrated potential for, effective university-level teaching. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of effective university teaching. Teaching interests or expertise in one or more of the following areas: digital marketing, marketing research, consumer behavior, or marketing analytics. Evidence of an active research pipeline and potential for sustained scholarly productivity. Interest or experience in applied and immersive learning. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues and contribute to a collegial, student-centered department. How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact: Department Chair, Jamye Foster ( jamye.foster@bsu.edu ) Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting application documents listed below. Only complete applications submitted through Workday will be considered. REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS: A cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the position A current résumé or curriculum vitae - Please do not use the Autofill feature for resume Academic philosophy highlighting how your candidacy aligns with Ball State University's values Within the application, please provide contact information for three professional references The option to upload your transcript is available but is not required at the time of application. Original, official transcripts from the issuing institution reflecting the highest related earned degree is required at the time of hire (even if your degree is obtained at Ball State University). This position will remain open until filled with the consideration date: September 27, 2026. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue until position is filled. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Biomedical-Program-Coordinator_R-02988": {
      "title": "Biomedical Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Biomedical Program Coordinator Compensation: $16.50 - 17.84 Department: Biology Start Date: 10/12/2026 About this opportunity: The Department of Biology is one of the largest and most academically active units within the College of Sciences and Humanities. Building on a long record of excellence in teaching, research, and service, the department provides rigorous, hands-on programs that prepare students for success in the biological and biomedical sciences. Biology hosts a robust graduate program and a large biomedical sciences undergraduate program. These programs require considerable communication and support for our students. The Department of Biology at Ball State University invites applications for a full-time Program Coordinator to assist the Directors of these programs. This is a full-time, 12-month position with the potential to be hybrid. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function The primary responsibility for this position is to provide administrative support for the Directors of the Masters, PhD, and Biomedical Sciences Programs. This includes assisting with all aspects of the programs and performing other duties as assigned by the Department Chairperson. Duties and Responsibilities: Manage Communications Respond to program inquiries and maintain student communication lists. Assist in tracking applicants through university systems (i.e. Stellic). Serve as a program communication liaison with faculty and administration. Assist with event planning Assist with organization/preparation of student orientation and faculty-student mixer events. Assist with organization and marketing of Fall Seminar Series. Assist with program management Assist with administration and tracking of TA evaluations. Assign student offices and maintain an office space inventory. Help to maintain program handbooks and websites. Participate in professional training and development as necessary. Act as back-up for the program directors. Manage applications and track student progress Manage student degree audit requests and maintain the accuracy of digital degree records, including processing exemptions and resolving record discrepancies Track applications. Assist with tracking student progress through the programs (coursework, milestones, paperwork). Perform other related duties as assigned. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. Minimum Qualifications: Associate degree in Biology, biomedical science, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. At least one year of office administrative/secretarial or related experience, Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite including Word, Excel, Outlook, and PowerPoint. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in biology, biomedical science, or a related field from an accredited institution. Experience with online portal software systems. How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact: Tim Carter tccarter@bsu.edu Important: Please follow the upload instructions for attaching all required documents listed below. NOTE: Do not use the autofill feature for your resume. Cover Letter Resume Applications must be received before 12:01 AM on September 23, 2026. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Temporary-Classroom-Aide_R-02703": {
      "title": "Temporary Classroom Aide",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Temporary Classroom Aide Compensation: 14.00 per hour Department: Burris Laboratory School - Temp A Start Date: 08/10/2026 About this opportunity:   Burris Laboratory Schools welcomes applications for Temporary Classroom aide. This position is part-time, working up to 30 hours per week. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Function : Burris Laboratory Schools welcomes applications for Temporary Classroom aide. This position is part-time, working up to 30 hours per week. Job Description : Work with K-12 students on a one-on-one basis in academic and social skills development. Provide small group assistance and instruction. Provide supervision during lunch times. Work collaboratively with administrators, faculty, parents, and students. Perform other related duties as assigned. Maintain regular and predictable attendance Minimum requirements : Must have a high school diploma or equivalent. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Preferred Education and Experience : Associates degree in related field How to apply:   Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: IMPORTANT: To ensure accurate processing of your application, do not rely on a resume upload to populate the job experience section. All work history must be entered directly into the application fields. Cover Letter Resume"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Postdoctoral-Researcher-in-Conservation-Genomics_R-02991": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Conservation Genomics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Researcher in Conservation Genomics Compensation: $62,374 Department: Biology About this opportunity: The Department of Biology has a Research Assistant position in conservation genomics. This is a full-time, at-will position with a start date of May 2027. This position is grant funded and the individual hired will have an at-will assignment. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Direct Chiricahua Leopard Frog breeding experiments at field sites during the summer and lead genomics projects during the academic year Job Duties: Field Research & Management - Direct and manage frog breeding experiments at the Southwestern Research Station (SWRS) and partner sites during the summer breeding seasons. Data & Laboratory Analysis - Organize and analyze genomic data, process genetic samples, and lead genomics work during the academic year. Collaboration - Integrate research efforts across academic and conservation partners. Supervise undergraduate researchers in the collection of frog development data and guide them in independent research experiences Dissemination & Planning - Participate fully in the planning and implementation of all research aims, present findings at scientific conferences, and lead the publication of research in peer-reviewed scientific journals. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in biology, conservation genomics, applied wildlife biology, evolution and ecology, or a closely related field by date of appointment. At least one year of research experience in a university setting. Preferred Qualifications: A blended background in conservation genomics and applied wildlife biology, with an interest in bioinformatics. Any experience with amphibian husbandry is helpful. Experience monitoring undergraduate researchers Strong collaborative skills for interacting with conservation agencies, non-profit organizations, and academic partners. Experience coordinating logistics for fieldwork or conducting research in remote areas. How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact Dr. Robert Denton, robert.denton@bsu.edu Important: Please follow the upload instructions for attaching all required documents listed below. NOTE: Do not use the autofill feature for the resume or CV. Cover Letter or CV Resume Applications must be received by September 29th, 2026, at 12:01 AM.  What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-ISOM_R-02051": {
      "title": "Instructor of ISOM",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of ISOM Compensation: $4,000 per class Department: Info Systems & Operations Mgt - Temp Start Date: 08/17/2026 About this opportunity:   The Information Systems & Operations Management Department in the Miller College of Business welcomes applications for part-time semester faculty appointments to teach undergraduate course(s). Candidates must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description : The Department of ISOM invites part-time semester faculty appointments to teach undergraduate course(s) in ISOM. The possibility for remote work will be considered. Please note that applications will remain active one year from the posting date. Therefore, if you apply for this position, you may not hear from the Department of ISOM until there is a need to hire an instructor to teach a specific course. Job duties and responsibilities: Teach undergraduate courses in ISOM department. Minimum qualifications: MBA or Master degree in a closely related field from an accredited institution by date of appointment. Minimum of 5 years working experience in the areas of teaching. Preferred qualifications: Ph.D. in related areas of teaching from an accredited institution. How to apply:   For inquires contact: ISOM@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below. IMPORTANT: To ensure accurate processing of your application, do not rely on a resume upload to populate the job experience section. All work history must be entered directly into the application fields. REQUIRED: 1. Curriculum Vitae or Resume 2. Contact information for 3 references 3. Cover Letter - optional but preferred Original transcripts, highest degree, required upon hire."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-Art--and-Design_R-02357": {
      "title": "Instructor of Art  and Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of Art  and Design Compensation: $3,000 - $9,000 Department: School of Art - Temp Start Date: 08/24/2026 About this opportunity:   The School of Art at Ball State University invites applications for part-time instructors to teach courses in Foundations or Studio Art. Successful candidates may be hired to teach between one and three sections. Teaching responsibilities are on campus, in Muncie, Indiana. Course development support and pedagogical mentoring will be offered. All instructors are expected to communicate regularly with students, provide meaningful and timely assessments, post course information on Canvas, and submit grades and other reports on time. The School of Art has over forty full-time faculty and staff and offers state-of-the-art facilities serving more than 700 undergraduate majors. Programs at the BA, BS, and BFA levels include art education, art history, graphic design, animation production, illustration, game art/design, visual effects, and a studio art program that includes drawing, painting, printmaking, ceramics, glass, metals + jewelry, sculpture, photography, and video and new media. School of Art students enjoy world-class facilities, with over 73,000 square feet of classroom, gallery, and studio space in the Art and Journalism Building, Applied Technology Building, and the Marilyn K. Glick Center for Glass. Students and faculty work closely with David Owsley Museum of Art on campus, among the finest university art collections in the nation. Ball State University is accredited by the National Association for Schools of Art and Design.  Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Applications will remain active for 1 year. Candidates may not hear from the school until there is a need to hire an instructor. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Description: Instructors of Art and Design will teach undergraduate courses in the Foundations (2D, 3D, 4D, or Drawing) and/or Studio Art program (drawing, painting, printmaking, ceramics, glass, metals + jewelry, sculpture, photography, video and new media), and/or other courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach between one and three undergraduate courses. Minimum Qualifications:   Master's degree in art, design, or related discipline by time of appointment.    Preferred Qualifications:   MFA degree in art, design, or related discipline by time of appointment. Engagement with contemporary art practices as an educator, artist, designer, and/or illustrator.  One year of teaching experience at the college level.   How to apply:   For inquiries   regarding   this opportunity, please contact:   Lara Kuykendall, Director,   lkuykendall@bsu.edu       IMPORTANT: To ensure accurate processing of your application, do not rely on a resume upload to populate the job experience section. All work history must be entered directly into the application fields. Required Documents: Cover letter   Curriculum vitae    Portfolio of up to 10 images of applicant’s creative work (saved as a single PDF with links to time-based work if applicable). If document size exceeds 10 MB, a link to portfolio may be provided.   Portfolio of up to 10 images of student work (saved as a single PDF with links to time-based work if applicable). If document size exceeds 10 MB, a link to portfolio may be provided.   Contact information (including email addresses) for three professional references. The option to upload transcripts is available. Original, official transcripts showing the highest related degree earned is required at the time of hire (even if obtained at BSU). Degree verification will be conducted."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Leadership-Organizational-Behavior_R-02774": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Leadership/Organizational Behavior",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Leadership/Organizational Behavior Compensation: $130,000 - $133,000 Department: Management Start Date: 08/01/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of Management in the Miller College of Business at Ball State University welcomes applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor with expertise in Leadership, Organizational Behavior, or related fields. Tenure status is not granted automatically; it is awarded based on demonstrated excellence in performance, budgetary considerations, tenure density, and the needs of the university. The university will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Position Function: Primary responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, conducting scholarly research in the areas of leadership, organizational behavior, or related fields, and service to the university and profession. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching: Teach up to 9 semester hours of undergraduate and/or graduate courses, both on-campus and online. Teaching reduction is available for exceptional research performance. Time release and summer stipend is available for recent PhD. graduates. Research: Conduct scholarly research, primarily in the area of leadership, organizational behavior, or related fields, and publish in high-quality academic journals. Service: Actively contribute in service roles to Ball State University, local community, and the academic profession.   Minimum Qualifications: Education: PhD from an AACSB-accredited institution in management or a closely related field with emphasis on leadership or organizational behavior topics. ABD candidates will be considered during the selection process. Experience: Evidence of scholarly research and teaching experience in business-related field. Teaching: At least one semester of higher education teaching experience in the field of management at an AACSB-accredited institution.   Preferred Qualifications: Teaching: At least one-year (9 months) of teaching experience in leadership, organizational behavior, or human resource management at an AACSB-accredited institution with preference for candidates that have interest and ability in teaching organizational change. Research: A record of publications in prestigious refereed journals in management. Service: Contributions to a prominent organization that serves academic professionals.   Required Certifications/Licensures: How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact: Dr. Abhishek Srivastava (abhishek.srivastava@bsu.edu) I mportant: Please follow upload instructions for attaching all required documents listed below . Only complete applications will be considered.  REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae - *Please do not use the Autofill feature for your resume/vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research agenda References - Within the application, you will be prompted to provide names and contact information for three (3) professional references. NOTE: Reference checks will not be conducted until the final round of the candidate selection process. This position will remain open until filled with a consideration date of September 15, 2026. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled.  What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-English-as-Another-Language_R-02795": {
      "title": "Instructor of English as Another Language",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of English as Another Language Compensation: $1,600.00 - $2,000.00 Department: Div of Lifetime Learning, NonCredit - Temp Start Date: 08/31/2026 About this opportunity:   We are seeking qualified, enthusiastic, and culturally competent candidates to join our Part-Time Adjunct Instructor Pool for Adult EAL (English as Another Language).  We offer 8-week cohorts throughout the year, with our next session starting at the end of August. Applicants admitted to this pool will be reviewed and hired on an as-needed basis prior to the start of each cohort. Our in-person classes are taught at different locations: Fishers, Indianapolis, and Whitestown. We are currently seeking faculty for the Fishers location.  This is a part-time temporary position teaching 32 hours total (2 hours, twice a week in the evenings) for 8 weeks. Continued teaching opportunities may be available. Salary will be based on experience. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: In this role, instructors facilitate dynamic, practical language instruction for adult learners aiming to improve their English for personal, professional, or academic goals. Position function and duties: Instruction:  Deliver engaging, learner-centered English lessons focusing on speaking, listening, reading, and writing for real-world adult contexts.  Lesson Preparation:  Plan and adapt curriculum to meet the diverse needs, skill levels, and cultural backgrounds of adult students.  Classroom Management:  Foster a safe, supportive, and inclusive learning environment where adult students feel confident practicing new skills.  Assessment & Tracking:  Monitor student progress, provide constructive feedback, and maintain accurate attendance records.  Communication:  Coordinate with program administrators regarding curriculum, student needs, and facility logistics. Minimum qualifications  Education:  Bachelor’s degree preferably in education, English, or TESOL  Experience:  Prior teaching experience  Skills:  Strong cross-cultural communication and interpersonal skills.  Flexibility, patience, and enthusiasm for working with adult learners.  Reliable transportation to your assigned location (Fishers, Indianapolis, or Whitestown). How to apply:   Submit your cover letter and cv. IMPORTANT: To ensure accurate processing of your application, do not rely on a resume upload to populate the job experience section. All work history must be entered directly into the application fields. If questions please contact Nell Hill at nrhill@bsu.edu"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Forensic-Science_R-02661": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Forensic Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Forensic Science Compensation: $65,000 - $75,000 Department: Criminal Justice & Criminology Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The College of Sciences and Humanities at Ball State University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level in forensic science. Preference will be given to individuals with practical experience in forensic science. The successful applicant will be housed in a department commiserate with the candidate’s expertise. A Ph.D. in forensic science, biology, chemistry, or forensic psychology or a closely related ﬁeld is required at the time of appointment. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching responsibilities comprise introductory and advanced courses in forensic science and/or courses in content areas that contribute to the forensic science program. Other teaching could include undergraduate and/or graduate courses in the home department. Applicants are expected to possess a strong commitment to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level and provide leadership in further forensic science program development. The selected candidate will also be expected to develop and maintain an independent and active research program, mentor student researchers, and provide service to the profession, university, and program. Minimum Qualifications: An earned Doctorate degree appropriate for a forensic science program, preferably in biology, chemistry, or a related ﬁeld by time of appointment. Research experience in a forensic science discipline or in methods and techniques adapted, supported, and employed by the forensic science community. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: The ability to establish effective collaborative relationships with a varied range of internal and external populations . Record of successful teaching in a college/university environment . Established scholarship record in forensic science, biology, chemistry, or forensic psychology . How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Dr. Benjamin Gibbs - Search Committee Chair brgibbs@bsu.edu,  765-285-5102 Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by October 1st, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Behavioral-Forensics--Psychology---Law-_R-02809": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Behavioral Forensics (Psychology & Law)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Behavioral Forensics (Psychology & Law) Compensation: Salary is commensurate with experience Department: Criminal Justice & Criminology Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The College of Sciences and Humanities at Ball State University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level in behavioral forensics (psychology & law). Preference will be given to individuals with doctoral training in clinical or counseling psychology whose research or teaching focuses on forensic or correctional applications. The successful applicant will be housed in a department of criminal justice and criminology. A Ph.D. in psychology with expertise in psychology and law or a closely related field is required at the time of appointment. Clinical and Counseling PhDs must be from APA or CPA accredited programs. Employer will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Description : The Forensic Science program at Ball State University seeks a tenure-track assistant professor to begin August 2, 2027. The successful applicant will teach psychology courses in the Behavioral Forensics concentration in our Forensic Science program; be able to establish an active research program that can involve students; and contribute to the service activities of the program and their respective disciplines. We are seeking applicants with expertise in psychology and law (e.g., forensic psychology, correctional psychology, or related areas). Support for this work is offered through research resources (e.g., EEG labs, funding opportunities; external grant supporting office); professional development opportunities (e.g., teaching training) and faculty mentorship. Duties and Responsibilities : Responsibilities include: Teach undergraduate psychology courses in the Forensic Science program (e.g., Forensic Psychology, Correctional Psychology, Psychology of Criminal Behavior, Psychopathology); remain current in and contribute to research in specialty area; contribute to the service activities of the program and their discipline. Minimum Qualifications : Ph.D. in psychology with expertise in psychology and law or related field from an accredited institution. ABDs will be considered if the doctorate is obtained by date of appointment. Clinical and Counseling PhDs must be from APA or CPA accredited programs Preferred Qualifications : Special consideration will be given to applicants with doctoral training in clinical or counseling psychology whose research or teaching focuses on forensic or correctional applications. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Dr. Benjamin Gibbs - Search Committee Chair brgibbs@bsu.edu, 765-285-5102 Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autoﬁll feature for resume: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by October 1st, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Instructors-of-Nutrition-and-Health-Science_R-02778": {
      "title": "Instructors of Nutrition and Health Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructors of Nutrition and Health Science Compensation: $3000-$9000 Department: Dept of Nutrition & Health Science - Temp Start Date: 08/17/2026 About this opportunity:   The Department of Nutrition and Health Science invites applications for part-time faculty semester appointments to teach classes in public health, research methods, or nutrition/dietetics; face-to-face on the Ball State campus in Muncie, Indiana OR online. Original official transcripts and licensure/credentials in respective field of expertise are required at time of hire. The applicant pool will be used for up to one year from the posting date to hire individuals. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Function : Teach face-to-face courses on the main campus in Muncie, Indiana, or online courses. Minimum Qualifications: For public health: Master’s degree or higher in public health, epidemiology, biostatistics, public health informatics, or related ﬁeld from an accredited institution by date of appointment Minimum of 1 year of successful on-campus university teaching experience or related work experience For research methods courses, professional experience in research is also needed, such as work for a research study in a funded research grant For nutrition/dietetics: Master’s degree or higher in nutrition or closely related field from an accredited institution by date of appointment Minimum of 1 year of successful on-campus university teaching experience or related work experience For research methods courses, professional experience in research is also needed, such as work for a research study in a funded research grant For medical nutrition therapy courses, RDN required Preferred Qualifications: Additional years of successful college or university teaching experience and/or work experience, including research experience. How to apply:   For inquiries, please contact : Dr. Alyce Fly, Chairperson – adfly@bsu.edu , 765-285-1502 Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume. 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae In support of your application for this position, please prepare and submit a cover letter that describes how your qualifications and experience align with the elements of the position description (or leadership profile)."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Temporary-Burris-Athletic-Coach_R-02749-1": {
      "title": "Temporary Burris Athletic Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Temporary Burris Athletic Coach Compensation: $500-$6,0000, based on coaching role Department: Burris Laboratory School - Temp A Start Date: 07/20/2026 About this opportunity:   Burris Laboratory School is seeking part-time, temporary athletic coaches to support and mentor students on various teams. Hours will include evenings and some weekends. Compensation is determined by specific role and responsibilities and normal range is $500.00-$6000.00 for the season. Candidates for this position must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position function : Provide coaching and training to student athletes. ​ Duties/Responsibilities: Coaching and Training: Develop and implement training programs Student Development : Help students establish personal and team goals. Game Management : Plan game strategies, select players Safety and Compliance: Ensure a safe environment for athletes, adhere to all school and safety standards, complete required safety training and implement necessary. Promote sportsmanship among athletes. Administrative Tasks: record keeping and reporting to school administrators and athletic director. Minimum Education and Experience : High school diploma or equivalent Knowledge of applicable sport Must be able to effectively communicate to students, parents, officials, school administration. How to apply:   For Inquiries, please contact: Athletic Director, Mack Rathbun: mack.rathbun@bsu.edu Required Documents:   Resume   Cover letter-optional but preferred   Three references should be provided     IMPORTANT: To ensure accurate processing of your application, do not rely on a resume upload to populate the job experience section. All work history must be entered directly into the application fields.      Requires successful completion of a background check and education verification."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-Nursing_R-02689": {
      "title": "Instructor of Nursing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of Nursing Compensation: $3,000 to $12,000 Department: School of Nursing - Temp Start Date: 08/17/2026 About this opportunity:   The School of Nursing welcomes applications from Master’s or Doctoral-prepared nurse educators with clinical experience for part-time, adjunct faculty positions for the baccalaureate program. Work assignments, days, times, and locations vary. The School has clinical instructional opportunities for well-qualified nurse educators Tues. through Sun. - morning, afternoon, and evening - in our expanding undergraduate program. Candidates must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Please note, if you apply for this position, you may not hear from the department until there is a need to hire an instructor. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: Part-time, contract faculty member with appropriate nursing specialization to teach in undergraduate courses. Work assignments, days, times, and locations vary. Faculty responsibilities include teaching in classroom, clinical, and/or simulation environments in baccalaureate courses for adult health, medical-surgical, psychiatric mental health, pediatrics, critical care, childbearing families, and other courses as appropriate. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach in classroom, clinical, and/or simulation environments in baccalaureate courses. Keep abreast of recent developments in nursing and incorporate into teaching. Actively contribute to the professional life of the School of Nursing, the College of Health, and Ball State University. Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in nursing from an accredited college or university by the date of appointment; AND Clinical nursing experience in area of teaching; AND Ability to communicate effectively Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience in higher education; Earned doctorate in nursing or related field from an accredited college or university. Required Certifications/Licensures: Current unencumbered State of Indiana Registered Nurse License by date of appointment. How to apply:   Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: IMPORTANT: To ensure accurate processing of your application, do not rely on a resume upload to populate the job experience section. All work history must be entered directly into the application fields. REQUIRED: Curriculum Vitae or Resume Contact information for 3 references Cover Letter - In your cover letter, please include the following information: • Your interest in teaching in-person, online, or both; Specific days and times, including weekends and evenings if applicable, you would be available to teach an in-person clinical section. RN licensure documentation Please bundle your documents into one document to ensure that you can include all required items. OPTIONAL: Transcripts (will be required upon hire) NP Certification Please note that RN licensure documentation must contain applicant’s name, license number, and current license expiration date, and be a copy, scan, or screenshot from an authoritative source. Questions about the opportunity can be directed to nursing@bsu.edu."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-School-of-Kinesiology_R-02683": {
      "title": "Instructor-School of Kinesiology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor-School of Kinesiology Compensation: $1,000-$3,000 Department: School of Kinesiology - Temp Start Date: 08/24/2026 About this opportunity:   The School of Kinesiology at Ball State University is seeking part-time semester instructors who are qualified to teach face-to-face or online courses in one or more of the following disciplines: aquatics, exercise science, physical education, sport administration, sport and exercise psychology, biomechanics, athletic coaching education, exercise physiology, or athletic training. This is a temporary position for 1-6 credit-hours per semester. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. The applicant pool will be used for up to one year from the posting date to hire individuals. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: The School of Kinesiology at Ball State University is seeking part-time semester instructors who are qualified to teach face-to-face or online courses in one or more of the following disciplines: aquatics, exercise science, physical education, sport administration, sport and exercise psychology, biomechanics, athletic coaching education, exercise physiology, or athletic training.  Job Responsibilities and Duties:  Teach courses from one to three credit hours each.  Create a standardized syllabus. Be available to students. Manage Canvas course site and submit grades. Also, under the direction of the Program Coordinator: Develop and manage syllabus materials. The adjunct Instructor is responsible for selecting and compiling tests, assignments and/or online discussion exercises that permit measurement of performance relative to course learning objectives and student learning outcomes. Coordinate courseware and curriculum with the Program Coordinator. The adjunct Instructor is responsible for reviewing any textbook and other courseware changes with the Program Coordinator and other full-time faculty teaching the course. Facilitate class instruction. The adjunct Instructor is responsible for teaching the assigned class in accordance with learning objectives and student learning outcomes. Administer evaluations of student performance based on course deliverables and course rubrics. Minimum Qualifications: For undergraduate classes, earned master's degree from an accredited college or university by time of appointment in aquatics, exercise science, physical education, sport administration, kinesiology, health education, or closely related field (must have a minimum of 18 credit-hours of graduate courses in the relevant discipline); for graduate classes, must have earned a terminal degree from an accredited college or university by time of appointment (unless approved through our School's approved tested experience policy).  Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience in a college setting.  Prior work experience in respective field of expertise. Licensure or credentials in respective field of expertise. How to apply:   For inquiries: Contact the School of Kinesiology at 765-285-8746 or sok@bsu.edu. Required Documents: Resume/CV Cover letter In support of your application for this position, please prepare and submit a cover letter that describes how your qualifications and experience align with the elements of the position description. Please include licensure/credentials and names and contact information for 3 references in your cover letter or resume/CV. IMPORTANT: To ensure accurate processing of your application, do not rely on a resume upload to populate the job experience section. All work history must be entered directly into the application fields. Original official transcripts and proof of licensure/credentials in respective field of expertise are required at time of appointment."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Teaching-Professor_R-02633": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor Compensation: $45,000 - $55,000 Department: History Start Date: 01/01/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of History at Ball State University offers undergraduate students’ courses to fulfill their course of study for their major, minor, or core curriculum. The position of oral historian will teach classes to gather information from informants through immersive learning projects. The results of these projects will be collected and stored in the university library and shared through community partners Full time - 40 hrs. per week Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: Using the master syllabus create a course syllabus and Canvas page, create in person instruction, perform assessment including midterms and finals, record and maintain documents. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. or ABD in history or related field by date of appointment. Experience with oral history in modern world history, and commitment to immersive learning instructional practices (see website). Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching HIST 152 Modern world history   How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Ronald Morris at rvmorris@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume: Curriculum Vitae Teaching evaluations if available Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by October 5th, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
