    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Part-Time-Bus-Driver-1_R-02754": {
      "title": "Part Time Bus Driver-1",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Part Time Bus Driver-1 Compensation: $20.83 - $20.83 Department: General Institutional Support Start Date: 08/03/2026 About this opportunity: At Ball State University our Part Time Bus Drivers will operate Ball State University buses to transport students, faculty, staff, and personnel on the shuttle run or other dispatched runs. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. WORK SHIFT: Monday to Friday; 12:30 p.m. - 6:30 p.m.; estimated at 27.5 hours per week for shuttle What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function Operate Ball State University buses to transport students, faculty, staff, and personnel on the shuttle run or other dispatched runs.   Duties & Responsibilities 1) Operate passenger buses, shuttles, vans and para-transit units on various routes as established by the Transportation Office. Requires the physical ability to sit for extended periods of time, operate various size/types of vehicles, move in and out of various vehicles to assist passengers, including disabled passengers, bend, grasp, finger and exert up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds of force constantly. Task requires a wide field of vision and the visual ability to perceive depth and distinguish colors. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, vibrations, etc. Task requires the mental ability to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions, information, and traffic signs and signals, and to receive, comprehend, and follow oral instructions and information.   2) Inspect buses and report any equipment malfunctions; maintain cleanliness of vehicles. Requires the physical ability to bend, stoop, hear, crawl, push, pull, walk, kneel, see, lift hoods of vehicles, and exert up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth and distinguish color. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, etc. Task requires the mental ability to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information, and to receive, comprehend, and follow oral instructions and information.   3) Fuel daily and inspect bus for any exterior damage. Requires physical ability to bend, stoop, push, pull, walk, kneel, see, lift hoods of vehicles, and exert up to 50pounds of force occasionally, 25 pounds of force frequently, and 10 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to read and check gauges, fluid levels, etc., perceive depth, and distinguish colors. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, oils, chemicals, etc. Task requires the mental ability to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information, and receive, comprehend, and follow oral instructions and information.   4) Maintain contact with Transportation Office when necessary via radio and/or telephone; inform office of changes in location, delays, traffic problems, emergencies, etc. Requires the physical ability to talk, hear, see, grasp, finger, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires a wide field of vision and the visual ability to perceive depth. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information, and receive, comprehend, and follow oral instructions and information.   5) Maintain accurate records of mileage and number of passengers; complete various trip sheets and logs foreach assigned task. Requires the physical ability to grasp, finger, write, see and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires visual ability to perceive depth, and read gauges and written materials. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information, and receive, comprehend, and follow oral instructions and information.   6) Assist and direct disabled individuals on and off vehicles as needed. Requires the physical ability to lift wheelchairs and individuals of various weight and height, grasp, finger, see, bend, stoop, reach, push, pull, talk, hear, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires a wide field of vision and visual ability to perceive depth. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, moving mechanical parts, noise, vibration, etc. Task requires the mental ability to read, comprehend, and follow written instructions and information, and receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions.   7) Report any problems with routes and make recommendations for changes when appropriate. Requires the physical ability to see, talk, write, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires mental ability to analyze situations, and provide written and oral information.   8) Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Requirements 1. High School Diploma or Equivalent (GED) 2. At least six months of verified professional driving experience. 3. Must demonstrate ability to drive bus (on-site driving test). 4. Must possess and maintain a valid CDL (Commercial Driver’s License) with an endorsement for public passengers and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. 5. Must possess a good driving record; verification through Bureau of Motor Vehicles. 6. Must pass a post offer/pre-employment mandatory drug and alcohol test. 7. Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty.   Preferred Experience Over-the-road (OTR) bus or truck driving experience. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Mike Hill, Supervisor of Bus Operations at 765-285-6005, mdhill5@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume. Cover Letter (optional) Resume (Required)"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Psychological-Science_R-02900": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychological Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Psychological Science Compensation: $65,000-$75,000. Department: Psychological Science Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of Psychological Science at Ball State University welcomes applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position to begin August 2027. The successful applicant will teach in our undergraduate psychological science major and master’s program in psychology, have a research program that complements our department’s current research interests and that involves undergraduate and graduate students, and contribute to the service activities of our department and discipline. We are seeking applicants who teach and conduct research in clinical or counseling psychology, particularly psychopathology, personality, psychological assessment, health psychology, and/or research/methodology courses. The position is open until filled with a consideration date of Dec. 1, 2026. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration. Employers will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Description:  The Department of Psychological Science at Ball State University seeks a tenure-track assistant professor to begin August 10, 2027. The successful applicant will be interested in teaching courses for our undergraduate psychological science major and master’s program in psychology; have a research program that will complement current research interests in the department and that can involve both undergraduate and graduate students; and contribute to the service activities of the department and discipline. We are seeking applicants who conduct research and teach in clinical or counseling psychology. Special consideration will be given to applicants who can teach one or more of the following: psychopathology, personality, psychological assessment, health psychology, and research/methodology courses. Our department includes twenty-one full-time faculty members who deliver excellent teaching, conduct high-quality research, and foster student-faculty mentorships. Support for this work is offered through research resources (e.g., grant supporting office ); professional development opportunities (e.g., teaching training) and faculty mentorship.  Duties and Responsibilities : Responsibilities include: teach graduate and undergraduate classes in the Department of Psychological Science programs; supervise graduate and/or undergraduate student research (e.g., honors theses); remain current in and contribute to research in specialty area; contribute to the service activities of the department and discipline.  Minimum Qualifications : Ph.D. in psychology or related field from an accredited institution. ABDs will be considered if the doctorate is obtained by date of appointment. Clinical and Counseling PhDs must be from APA or CPA accredited programs.   Preferred Qualifications:   Special consideration will be given to applicants who can teach one or more of the following: psychopathology, personality, psychological assessment, health psychology, and research/methodology courses. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Kristen Ritchey at karitchey@bsu.edu. Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume: Cover Letter. In support of your application for this position, please submit a cover letter that describes how your qualifications and experiences align with the elements of the position description. Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement (e.g., teaching interests, teaching philosophy) Research Statement  Finalists may be asked to submit additional documents (e.g., letters of recommendation, teaching evaluations).  Optional Documents: Transcripts Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by December 1st, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Administrative-Coordinator_R-03175-1": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Administrative Coordinator Compensation: $16.50 - 17.84 Department: Info Systems & Operations Mgt (Qiannong Start Date: 09/21/2026 About this opportunity: The Department of Information Systems and Operations Management invites applications for an Administrative Coordinator. This multifaceted position offers the opportunity to collaborate with faculty, staff, and students while managing office operations, coordinating budgets, supervising student employees, and supporting departmental initiatives. The successful candidate is highly organized, detail-oriented, and possesses strong communication skills enabling them to thrive in a fast-paced environment. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Coordinate all departmental office operations; manage administrative workflow; supervise students and office-assigned graduate assistants. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Oversee and organize office operations; perform administrative and secretarial duties; assist the department Chair in the preparation of a variety of college and university reports concerning such activities as program reviews, accrediting agency documentation, assignment reports and equipment requests. 2. Monitor budget records for all departmental accounts; submit online purchase orders and receipts of goods and services; verify monthly copier and telephone expenses; prepare expenditure projections for budget requests; coordinate and follow-up departmental equipment requisitions; maintain records and monitor equipment repair process. 3. Assist with class and instructor scheduling and course changes; negotiate space requests; input instructor updates and online permission approval; prepare postings for curricular revisions and new programs; process and record grade changes. 4. Maintain departmental records, personal files, and databases to ensure compliance with university regulations; coordinate documentation for processing employment contracts and other personnel related forms and records. 5. Manage and supervise department labs and student employees; security of lab facilities; scheduling and payroll; order lab supplies; maintain hardware and software inventory; coordinate computer classroom reservations. 6. Provide information to students and faculty regarding major/minor requirements, course scheduling, registration, etc.; assist the department Chair in implementing departmental policies and procedures; compose memos and correspondence for the department Chair; oversee the use of departmental resources. 7. Hire, train, assign, and evaluate student workers including graduate assistants; verify, monitor, and approve, work hours; act as liaison with other university offices, departments, and contacts from outside the university. 8. Perform receptionist duties; greet and assist visitors, answer telephone calls, answer inquiries, and direct individuals. 9. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. 10. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Associate’s degree or an additional two years of related experience will be accepted in lieu of an associate’s degree. At least one year of office administration or related experience. Proficiency with Microsoft Word and Excel. Strong communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree. Familiarity with Banner; experience working with budgets; supervisory experience. How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact: Dr. Chan Gu: qgu@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions for attaching all required supporting application documents listed below. Only complete applications will be considered. REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS: Cover Letter Resume - Please do not use the Autofill feature to upload resume) Application Deadline: 9/23/2026, 12:01 a.m. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Coordinator-of-Recreation-Operations-for-Competitive-Sports-and-Concession-Operations_R-02528": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Recreation Operations for Competitive Sports and Concession Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Coordinator of Recreation Operations for Competitive Sports and Concession Operations Compensation: $43,888-$43,888 Department: Recreation Services About this opportunity: The Coordinator of Recreation Operations for Competitive Sports and Concessions operations is housed within Ball State University’s division of Business and Auxiliary Services under the department of Recreation Services, which plays a vital role in fostering wellness, community, and active engagement across the campus ecosystem. Located in Muncie, Indiana, Ball State University is a world-class, comprehensive public research institution defined by its bold \"We Fly\" ethos, state-of-the-art facilities, and deep institutional ties to regional development. The campus is proudly woven into the fabric of Muncie, a historic, welcoming city of approximately 65,000 residents that serves as the county seat of Delaware County. Situated just an hour northeast of Indianapolis, the region beautifully balances a classic Midwest college-town energy with accessible urban amenities, featuring a rich cultural landscape—highlighted by the Minnetrista Museum & Gardens—and exceptional outdoor resources like the White River greenways and Prairie Creek Reservoir. Together, the university and the broader East Central Indiana community offer an incredibly affordable, tight-knit, and rewarding environment to live, work, and connect. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Provide support in all operational functions of Recreation Services. Areas include but are not limited to the management of student staff and situations in: aquatics, programs, facilities, marketing, membership services, Recreation Services events, and Sport Facilities events. Programs include but are not limited to: coverage of all programs (Learn to Swim, Family Swim, Master’s Swim, Youth and Family Programming and others), intramural sports, and club sport events. Ability to work nights and weekends. Duties and Responsibilities: Administer and further develop, plan, and coordinate a comprehensive university recreation program that includes but is not limited to Intramural Sports, Sport Clubs, Programs and Concession Operations. Other areas include the management of Recreation Services membership services, and event management. Management of other areas including but not limited to: Outdoor Pursuits Climbing Wall, Rental Center, Trips, Facilities, Aquatic Programming, Youth and Family, Marketing, Informal Programming, Rec Fit, Informal Recreation Spaces and other Recreation Services facilities and programs as needed. Recruit, hire, train, and develop staff such as student employees, while actively promoting and developing opportunities for those students. Manage the day-to-day operations of all facility related functions with Recreation Services and Concession Operations including but not limited to risk, financial compliance, travel, allocation of finances, purchasing, inventory management, and trademark compliance associated with the areas of Aquatics, Facilities, Intramural Sports Program, Sport Club Program,  Community Programs, and Concession Operations. Assist in the CPR/AED/First-Aid certification process for all staff and program participants. Provide an effective risk management plan for all areas of responsibility. Provide an environment that is safe, conducive for social fellowship, and meaningful interactions for all participants. Manage financial resources, including student and casual staff payroll, in accordance with university policies and procedures. Assist in the oversight of accurate accounting and management of all financial transactions associated with the areas of Aquatics, Facilities, Informal Programming, Intramural Sports, Sport Clubs, Community Programs, Youth and Family, Concession Operations, and Event Management. Develop annual goals and objectives, which accurately reflect the operations of the Office of Sports Facilities and Recreation Services, as well as the goals and mission of Ball State University. Develop, create, and maintain program reports for the areas of Aquatics, Facilities, Informal Programming, Intramural Sports, Sport Club Program, Community Programs, Concession Operations, and Event Management. Maintaining industry standards, evaluation, and assessment of all programs completed as assigned. Provide support in the procurement and management of equipment and supplies in all areas including Aquatics, Facilities, Informal Programming, Intramural Sports, Sport Clubs, Youth and Family Programs, Concession Operations, and Event Management. Provide on-call support throughout the course of the year to help in the oversight of all areas, events, or programs related to the Office of Sports Facilities and Recreation Services. Provide support to fellow Coordinators and Director of Recreation in other programs as assigned, including special event coverage and promotional events. Provide support with the management of full-time field facility attendants for custodial and event set-up and tear-down needs. Establish working relationships with individuals, university departments, organizations, as well as outside agencies and groups as assigned. Contribute and maintain professional leadership, communication, and positive behavior to all internal and external patrons. Behavior should serve as a positive reinforcement to the decisions, philosophies, and judgements of the Recreation Services leadership team. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution or an equivalent combination of education, credentials, certification and experience. At least one year of full-time recreation experience (a two-year graduate assistant position is equivalent to one year of experience, three years of undergraduate experience is equivalent to one year of experience). At least one year of direct management of student staff, facility risk management experience, or other university related programming. Must maintain and possess a valid driver’s license and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. American Red Cross Lifeguard Certification, American Red Cross Lifeguard Instructor Certification (LGI), American Red Cross CPR, AED, First-Aid Instructor. ServSafe Certification, and Indiana Employee Alcohol Permit. All certifications must be obtained within 90 days of employment but may be dependent upon available certification locations and dates. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in recreation administration, sport administration, or related field from an accredited Institution. At least two years of professional experience in college or university recreation Aquatics, Programs, Facilities, Intramural Sports, Club Sports, Concession Operations, and Event Management. Certified Pool Operating (CPO) License or equivalent. High School sports officiating certification(s). Active involvement in the Indiana Recreation Sports Association (IRSA). How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Ben Peak, bwpeak@bsu.edu Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below.  Im portant: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: 1. Resume Optional Document (Recommended for Best Consideration): 2. Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
