    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Director-of-Donor-Relations-and-Stewardship_R-03167": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Donor Relations and Stewardship",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Director of Donor Relations and Stewardship Compensation: $46,000 - $55,000 Department: BSU Foundation_O About this opportunity: Join Our Team: Assistant Director of Donor Relations and Stewardship Are you ready to be part of an energetic and unified team dedicated to transforming higher education? Our foundation is breaking down barriers between advancement, alumni relations, and stewardship to create a cohesive environment where philanthropy and innovative partnerships thrive. This is your chance to make a significant impact as we fulfill Our Call to Beneficence: The Campaign for Ball State University, aimed at elevating student support both financially and academically. Why Join Us? -Dynamic Team Environment: Collaborate with passionate professionals who are committed to our mission. -Cutting-Edge Initiatives: Be at the forefront of redefining philanthropy in education. -Unified Structure: Work within a seamless organization with no barriers between key departments. -Supportive Culture: A high-achieving work environment that values camaraderie and collaboration. -Impactful Work: A mission that changes lives through education and philanthropy. We invite you to join our team and make a difference. Join us in our mission to support students in realizing their purpose, achieving their dreams, and leading meaningful lives. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: The Assistant Director of Donor Relations and Stewardship contributes to the team’s overall goal of building a culture of gratitude and impact for and with donors, campus partners, and students. This individual will play a key role in managing and executing individualized stewardship for major and principal donors. This position provides comprehensive, high impact experiences to significant donors, proactively monitors and manages their stewardship needs, and maintains an accurate account of each donor’s involvement and ongoing activity. Stewardship projects may be complex and include multiple deliverables, including written communications, videos, or personalized interactions with University leadership, faculty, and staff.   The assistant director is someone who excels at project management, attention to detail, creative inquiry, and collaborative partnerships.     Duties/Responsibilities: Contribute to the Donor Relations and Stewardship team’s efforts to increase donor retention year over year overall and within key constituencies and gift bands through execution of a comprehensive donor relations and stewardship plan.   Work closely with the Director of Donor Relations and Stewardship, as well as development staff, to develop and implement personalized stewardship plans for assigned donors, based on their interests, giving history, and communication preferences plans. Plan and execute exclusive experiences that foster deeper connections between donors and the university.   Collaborate with donor relations staff to develop and deliver robust personalized fund and beneficiary reports for assigned donors. Ensure personalized reports contain compelling narratives and visuals and are accurate and error-free.   Use Raiser’s Edge NXT to document and track donor stewardship and engagement efforts.   Assist with managing the Foundation’s leadership annual giving society, including recognition efforts, stewardship communications, and events as needed.   Build and maintain strong relationships with internal stakeholders, such as development officers, faculty, and staff.   Stay current on evolving trends in donor relations, stewardship, and recognition overall. Connect with peers at other institutions and proactively participate in webinars and conferences that provide professional growth opportunities. Assist with the execution of Tier 1 initiatives and events related to donor experiences, including initiatives such as One Ball State Day, Homecoming, Power of Beneficence, and athletics VIP events, as needed.   Perform other related duties as assigned.   Must be able to work occasional evenings and weekends as may be required of the role.   Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in event management, public relations, marketing, communications, or a related field. A minimum of two years of experience in donor relations, annual giving, marketing, event planning, alumni engagement, project management or related field, or a combination of education and related experience. Demonstrated ability in working with campus partners, colleagues, volunteers, and/or clients both digitally and in person. Demonstrated experience in planning and executing university and/or non-profit events. Proven ability to work with a high level of independence, maintain confidentiality, prioritize assignments, and manage time effectively. Experience managing multiple projects and tasks simultaneously from the planning stages to execution and analysis. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel and PowerPoint Preferred Qualifications: Experience in major gift fundraising and/or with high-end constituent relationship management. Database management experience; familiarity with Raiser’s Edge preferred. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Assistant Director of Donor Relations and Stewardship Search Committee at foundation@bsu.edu . Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below.  Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: Resume Optional Document (Recommended for best consideration): Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Athletic-Trainer_R-03098": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Athletic Trainer Compensation: $45,000-$47,000 Department: Athletic Training About this opportunity: Join a dedicated team committed to supporting the health, safety, and success of NCAA Division I student-athletes. As an Assistant Athletic Trainer, you'll work directly with student-athletes and coaches in a collaborative, high-performing athletics department that values excellence, innovation, and student development. Ball State University offers a welcoming campus community, outstanding professional development opportunities, and the chance to make a meaningful impact on the lives of student-athletes every day. If you're passionate about sports medicine and want to be part of a department that strives to compete for championships while fostering student success, we'd love to hear from you. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Perform duties as assigned with the health care program and as directed by the Head Athletic Trainer. Duties & Responsibilities 1. Make recommendations for the coordination of the day-to-day operations of the health care program for Intercollegiate Athletics. 2. Serve as the athletic trainer and have direct supervision for one or more sports, as necessary on a daily basis, as assigned by the Head Athletic Trainer. 3. Evaluate injuries and make physician referral decisions for assigned sports. 4. Design and implement, in coordination with the team physician, all rehabilitation and therapeutic programs for assigned sports. 5. Work in conjunction with other members of the training staff, to supervise the athletic training students in the athletic training major. 6. Direct all communication between the athlete, training room staff, team physicians, and coaching staff for the assigned sports. 7. Coordinate with the Strength and Conditioning Coach regarding programs for injured and rehabilitating athletes. 8. Some teaching may be included as assigned by the Chair of the School of Physical Education, Sport, and Exercise Science. 9. Show commitment to and responsibility for, adherence to all rules and regulations of Ball State University, the Mid-American Conference and the NCAA. 10. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university by date of appointment; 2. NATA certification; Indiana Athletic Trainer State License or eligible for licensure. 3. At least two years of related experience. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Master's degree. 2. At least three years of related experience. How to apply: Please apply via the online Ball State University job portal . Please list three professional references within the online application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:  Do  not  use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: ·         Resume Optional Document: ·         Cover Letter   detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
