    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Director-of-Biomedical-Programs_R-02975": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Biomedical Programs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Director of Biomedical Programs Compensation: $57,000 - $60,000 Department: Biology About this opportunity: The Department of Biology at Ball State University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Director of the Biomedical Sciences Program. This is a full-time, in-person, 12-month professional position. The Department of Biology is one of the largest and most academically active units within the College of Sciences and Humanities. Building on a long record of excellence in teaching, research, and service, the department provides rigorous, hands-on programs that prepare students for success in the biological and biomedical sciences. Students in the biomedical sciences constitute about 40% of the nearly 850+ majors in the Biology Department. Career readiness, mentoring, and advising are all key elements of our students’ journey. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: The primary responsibility for this position is to assist with implementing the Biomedical Sciences program. This includes guiding and managing the program as well as mentoring and advising undergraduates in the program and performing other duties as assigned by the Department Chairperson. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach and assist in the career readiness courses in career readiness courses. Advise students on academics and professional school application preparedness. Develop and deliver workshops, guest speakers, and other professional development opportunities in line with the focus of student programs. Coordinate with the undergraduate curriculum coordinator on program changes and requirements. Participate in recruitment and retention events (may include some evenings and weekends). Support the Director with data gathering, analysis, and report generation. Stay up to date with trends and changes in professional schools and pre-health professions advising via trainings, workshops, and webinars. Perform additional related duties as assigned by the Department Chairperson. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in Biology, biomedical sciences, or a related field from an accredited institution by date of appointment. At least one year of managerial experience in the biomedical or related field. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Biology, biomedical sciences, or a related field from an accredited institution. Experience teaching or advising at the university level. Demonstrated knowledge of and experience working with diverse learners. Familiarity with the application processes for health professions programs and schools. Experience partnering with biomedical agencies. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Dr. Tim Carter at tccarter@bsu.edu. Please follow the upload instructions to attach all of the required documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume. Cover letter Resume or CV Applications must be received before 12:01 AM on September 24, 2026. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
