    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Lecturer-of-Interior-Design_R-00854": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer of Interior Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-10-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Lecturer of Interior Design Compensation: The salary pay range for this position begins at $48,000 Department: Department of CMID Start Date: 01/05/2026 About this opportunity: The Department of Construction Management and Interior Design has a full-time non-tenure track faculty position for the Interior Design program available January 2026. Primary responsibilities include teaching 12 credit hours per semester in the area of interior design and participating in department, college and university service tasks as needed. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: - Teach 12 credit hours of undergraduate or graduate online courses per semester.  - Assist in obtaining and/or maintaining the Council for Interior Design Accreditation.  - Develop new courses, as needed and/or revise existing courses.  - Participating in department, college and university service tasks as needed. Minimum Qualifications: - Master's degree from an accredited institution in Interior Design, Architecture, or closely related field. - Three years of experience in the design industry. - Evidence of excellent teamwork. For faculty qualified through tested experience, the following guidelines will be considered in lieu of the stated minimum qualifications: - A minimum of five (5) years of experience. - Experience at the managerial/professional level. - Relevant professional licensure and certification(s) may include but are not limited to: 1.Registered as an Interior Designer, or Architect (RA) 2. National Council for Interior Design Qualification (NCIDQ) Certification 3. Accreditation as a Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design Accredited Professional (LEED-AP) Preferred Qualifications: - Master's degree in interior design, architecture, or closely related field. - Experience with design software programs: Revit, CAD, SketchUp, Rhino, Lumion, etc.. - Experience in design build. - Experience in construction management. - Licensure and/or certification in interior design (NCIDQ), Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design Professional (LEED-AP), or closely related field. - A record of successful teaching experience, as demonstrated through reappointment to teaching positions, student evaluations, peer evaluations and/or administrative evaluations. - More than five years of experience in design and/or the interior design industry. - Effective oral and written communication. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Dr. Sarah Angne Alfaro at smangnealfar@bsu.edu or 765-285-2466. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Required Documents 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae (Do not use the \"autofill\" resume feature) 3. Portfolio (or link to website) including personal design work and/or evidence of teaching Optional Documents 1. Undergraduate Transcripts 2. Master's Transcripts Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by: October 28, 2025, at 12:01 A.M. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Heat-Plant-Group-Leader_R-03244": {
      "title": "Heat Plant Group Leader",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Heat Plant Group Leader Compensation: $42.00 - $42.00 Department: Heat Plant Operations Start Date: 09/18/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Facilities Planning and Management has an opportunity to work on the beautiful campus. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefits package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, university-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more. The ideal candidate will be flexible, and will possess great service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on campus opportunity. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. 3rd Shift 11:00 p.m. to 7:00 a.m. Sunday through Thursday What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under general supervision, direct, lead, assign and perform duties related to inspection, maintenance, repair, replacement, and operation of all heat plant equipment, insuring compliance with EPA, OSHA, and all appropriate operating regulations and codes. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Test water samples with chemicals and equipment; adjust chemical supplies in water depending on results of test. Requires the physical ability to stand, stoop, crouch, kneel, grasp, finger, lift, reach, climb, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to read and interpret related Heating Plant instrumentation, perceive depth, and distinguish color. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, related testing equipment, barrel truck, hand truck, etc. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information, and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 2. Record tests and treatment data. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, finger, grasp, stand and/or walk for extended periods of time, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth and distinguish color. Task requires the ability to operate related testing equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, heights, and confined spaces. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 3. Assign and perform work related to maintenance, repair, and cleaning of the Heat Plant equipment. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, talk, hear, stand and/or walk for extended periods of time, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth, read and interpret diagrams, schematics, and related Heating Plant instrumentation, and distinguish color. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, welding machines, cutting torches, etc. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 4. Train Heat Plant staff in procedures for operation, maintenance, and repair of equipment. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, talk, hear, stand and/or walk for extended periods of time, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth and read and interpret related Heating Plant instrumentation. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, welding machines, cutting torches, related testing equipment, etc. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions, training reports, and information. 5. Inspect tunnels and equipment for condition and recommend maintenance projects Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, talk, hear, stand and/or walk for extended periods of time, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth and read and interpret related Heating Plant instrumentation. Task requires the ability to operate hand tools, ladders, and scaffolds. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 6. Acts for supervisor when assigned. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, push, pull, lift, finger, grasp, talk, hear, stand and/or walk for extended periods of time, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and up to 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth, distinguish colors, and read and interpret related Heating Plant instrumentation. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, office equipment, and computer keyboard. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 7. Evaluate and provide feedback on work performance of assigned employees. Requires the physical ability to walk, stand, talk, hear, grasp, finger, lift, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth and distinguish color. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 8. Acquire and maintain knowledge of various job related chemicals, environmental concerns, and current technological improvements/advancements. Requires the physical ability to walk, stand, talk, hear, grasp, finger, lift, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to read small print, perceive depth, and distinguish color. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 9. Read and comprehend blueprints, drawings, diagrams, and sketches to insure proper specifications are followed. Requires the physical ability to stand, talk, hear, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color, read small print, and perceive depth. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 10. Perform other duties as assigned. May require any or all of the above mentioned abilities. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent (GED ). 1.Successful completion of an apprenticeship program as Stationary Engineer as approved by the Bureau of Apprenticeship and Training, or at least six (6) years of experience in operation and maintenance of a coal, gas, and oil fired boiler plant or related equipment, or equivalent combination of education and experience from which comparable job knowledge can be acquired as determined by Ball State University. 2.Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, University policies, procedures, and communications, and perform mathematical calculations. 3.Must possess and maintain a valid Driver’s License and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. . 4. Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty. 5.You must be 18 years or older. Preferred Qualifications: Vocational school training 1.Supervisory experience. 2. Over six (6) year’s experience. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Devon Johnson, Assistant Manager of Plant Operations at 765-285-6176 or devon.johnson@bsu.edu . Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Optional documents (Recommended for best consideration). Resume Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Nurse-Practitioner_R-03202": {
      "title": "Nurse Practitioner",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Nurse Practitioner Compensation: $60/hour Department: Interprofessional Community Clinics - Temp Start Date: 10/16/2026 About this opportunity:   Join Ball State University’s College of Health as a part-time Nurse Practitioner with the Healthy Lifestyle Center, part of the Interprofessional Community Clinics. This unique position offers the opportunity to provide high-quality, patient-centered care while working alongside professionals and students in an innovative, interprofessional clinical environment. We are seeking a collaborative, community-focused provider who is passionate about a model of care that values prevention, wellness, and whole-person health. Depending on the provider’s background and area of expertise, there may also be opportunities to help develop and expand clinical services to meet the evolving needs of our patients and community. The successful candidate will help individuals live healthier lives, expand access to care in East Central Indiana, and prepare the next generation of healthcare professionals through hands-on clinical mentorship. This Rural Health Transformation Program is supported by the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) of the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) as part of a financial assistance award totaling $206,927,896.80 with 100 percent funded by CMS/HHS. The contents are those of the author(s) and do not necessarily represent the official views of, nor an endorsement, by CMS/HHS, or the U.S. Government. Qualifying candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: The College of Health and our Interprofessional Community Clinics invites passionate and community-focused Nurse Practitioners to join the Healthy Lifestyle Center as a part-time provider delivering high-quality care across the lifespan. This is a unique opportunity to practice in a mission-driven clinical setting where innovation, collaboration, and service come together to improve lives. The successful candidate will play a vital role in expanding access to comprehensive care for individuals and families in East Central Indiana while mentoring future healthcare professionals and contributing to an interprofessional model of care that values prevention, wellness, and whole-person health. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Provide comprehensive medical services to patients across the lifespan. Conduct health histories, physical examinations, diagnostic evaluations, and treatment planning. Diagnose and manage acute and chronic conditions. Prescribe medications and therapies in accordance with regulatory standards. Deliver preventive services, wellness counseling, and patient education. Collaborate with staff and students in an interprofessional clinical environment. Coordinate patient care and referrals as needed. Serve as a clinical preceptor and mentor to healthcare students. Maintain accurate and timely electronic health records. Participate in quality improvement and patient safety initiatives. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree or higher in Nursing from an accredited institution. Current Indiana licensure as a Nurse Practitioner or eligible. National certification as a Nurse Practitioner or eligible. Current DEA registration or ability to obtain. Demonstrated experience in practice within the field of certification. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in an interprofessional clinical environment or community health setting. Experience supervising or mentoring students. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Work Environment: This position is based in the Interprofessional Community Clinics and community-based rural training clinics and involves direct patient care, student supervision, and collaboration with interdisciplinary teams in a learning-centered environment. How to apply:   Applications must be submitted through Ball State University’s Workday system. Interested candidates should upload the following materials: Cover letter outlining interest in the position and alignment with the mission of the Interprofessional Community Clinics Current curriculum vitae or resume (do not use the Autofill resume feature) Current nursing license indicating advanced practice status within the field of specialization Proof of current national certification as an advanced practice registered nurse Optional: a portfolio containing any additional documents relevant to your application for this opportunity Three references are required"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Senior-Broadcast-Engineer_R-02471": {
      "title": "Senior Broadcast Engineer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Senior Broadcast Engineer Compensation: $22.00 - 24.20 Department: University Media Services_A Start Date: 10/21/2026 About this opportunity: This is an opportunity to join the Ball State University Media Services department’s Engineering team. This full-time opportunity comes with an attractive benefits package, including health insurance, which includes dental and prescription coverage, discounts on University amenities and cultural events, retirement, and much more. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Perform the duties of Senior Broadcast Engineer and ensure broadcast media equipment is properly maintained to minimize downtime. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Provide engineering support for remote media productions and presentations, including teleconferences, sporting events, satellite uplinks, and downlinks, and streaming to multiple platforms. Perform duties as a remote/studio engineer; assist operators and clients with the operation of equipment; upgrade, install, and maintain equipment for UMS and other departments on campus. 2. Provide engineering support for microwave links, satellite uplinks, and downlinks, fiber optics systems, including SMPTE, single-mode and multi-mode fiber, and networking equipment. Knowledge and expertise in the use of networking and streaming hardware and software. 3. Install, maintain, and repair broadcast equipment for University Media Services; includes WIPB, WBST, WCRD, WCRH, and other university departments. 4. Install, configure, and maintain campus digital signage systems, players, and monitors. Work with departments and facilities for proper installation and operation. 5. Lead, design, implement, and maintain broadcast control rooms, video news media labs, and recording studio audio suites. Work as a system administrator for rack rooms in each area. On-call for equipment maintenance and functionality during high-traffic times. 6. Use complex software and hardware systems, including Networking setup and configuration, Windows, AutoCAD, Microsoft Office Suite, Presentations, scheduling programs, interfacing practices, programming, robotic systems, 3d Printers, PC, MAC, Linux system platforms. 7. Work directly with faculty, staff, and administrators to ascertain needs for new and renovated teaching facilities, document the requirements and suggestions, provide product and vendor recommendations, provide budget consultation and project management, provide as-built documentation, and coordinate with vendors for ongoing maintenance, upgrades, and technical support. 8 . Set up, check, operate, and monitor equipment for studio and remote productions; includes equipment for distance learning programs as well as academic and promotional productions. 9. Work in interdepartmental teams on production work, engineering work, quality control, work evaluations of members, scheduling, solving problems, and commercial broadcast productions. 10 . Apply thorough knowledge of the use of complex electronic test equipment such as oscilloscopes, computerized signal generators, voltmeters, waveform monitors, fiber test equipment, and knowledge of the safe operation and use of other specialized test equipment. 11 . Monitor procedures and ensure quality of work, document standard operating procedures, and oversee the continuous update of systems as necessary. 12 . Perform component-level repair of media-related equipment for Ball State University’s campus, including electrical and soldering requirements. Must be able to read and interpret diagrams. 13 . Provide engineering support for the university cable system by maintaining and repairing the MATV system and equipment. 14 . Direct interaction with students during the broadcast of sporting events, studio shoots, and other remote broadcast and streaming events. Includes continual training, supervising, and instruction of students in the proper use of broadcast equipment and game day operations. Provide knowledge and training to practicum students in one-on-one sessions throughout the semester as needed by the Department of Media. 15. Perform other related duties as assigned. 16. Maintain regular and predictable attendance as required by this position. Minimum Qualifications:    Associate’s degree in electronics or related area or equivalent. Over three through five years of related experience; strong computer skills. Must possess and maintain a valid driver’s license and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy; strong computer skills. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Bob Rickner, Manager of UMS Engineering, at the following email address:  brickner@bsu.edu Please list three professional references within the online application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Please follow the upload instructions to attach all required supporting documents listed below. Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
