    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Educational-Psychology--Tenure-Line-_R-03287": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Educational Psychology (Tenure-Line)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Educational Psychology (Tenure-Line) Compensation: $70,000-$75,000 Department: Educational Psychology Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The Ball State University Department of Educational Psychology invites applications for a 9-month tenure-line faculty position in Quantitative Psychology/Quantitative Methodology. The department seeks a scholar with expertise in advanced quantitative methods who will contribute to graduate instruction, methodological research and consultation, interdisciplinary collaboration, and externally funded research. Expertise in emerging methodologies, particularly machine learning and data mining, is highly desirable. The successful candidate will teach graduate courses in statistics, quantitative methods, and research methodology in both in-person and online formats. The position will play an important role in the M.S. in Quantitative Psychology and Ph.D. in Educational Psychology programs through student advising, mentoring of master’s capstone projects, and service on doctoral committees. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active program of scholarship, pursue opportunities for external funding, and provide service to the department, college, university, and profession. The faculty member will also contribute methodological expertise to faculty research and collaborative projects within the department and across the university. This position offers substantial opportunities for interdisciplinary research and methodological collaboration. We seek a collegial scholar who will contribute to the continued development of the Quantitative Psychology program and expand the department’s methodological expertise in response to evolving research and workforce demands. Rank and salary are commensurate with qualifications and experience. Summer teaching and administrative stipends may be available consistent with university policy. The university will consider sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching Teach three graduate-level research methodology/statistical analysis courses each fall and spring. Courses may be scheduled on campus or online. Scheduled course content could cover: Introductory Statistics Research Methodology ANOVA methodology Multiple Regression Multivariate Statistics/Data Mining Categorical Data Analysis Factor Analysis Latent Variable Modeling Psychometric/Measurement theory Longitudinal Data Analysis Multilevel Data Analysis Scholarship Maintain an active research agenda resulting in dissemination through publication in refereed journals and presentation at conferences. Grant writing and statistical consulting are also desirable. Service Lead curriculum review and continuous program improvement in MS in Quan psychology. Actively engage in university and professional service. Advisement of Masters and Doctoral Level capstone/thesis projects. Serve as a member of department, college and university committees and act as a supportive and collaborative colleague engaging in department discussion and endeavors. ​ Minimum Qualifications: Earned doctorate in Quantitative Psychology, Educational Psychology, Statistics, Research Methodology, Measurement, or a closely related field by date of appointment. At least one semester (4 months) of demonstrated experience mentoring, advising graduate students, with the ability to contribute to master’s thesis and doctoral dissertation committees. At least one semester (4 months) regarding evidence of, or potential for, effective teaching of graduate-level quantitative methods/statistics courses. Evidence of, or potential for, an active program of scholarship in quantitative methodology or its applications. Preferred Qualifications: Expertise in machine learning, data mining, and/or computational quantitative methods, particularly applications related to AI and large or complex datasets. Expertise in one or more additional areas such as psychometrics, latent variable modeling/structural equation modeling, Bayesian analysis, categorical or multivariate analysis, or meta-analysis. Experience teaching advanced quantitative methods at the graduate level, including online instruction. Evidence of successful interdisciplinary research collaboration and methodological consultation. Experience contributing quantitative/methodological expertise to externally funded research. How to apply: For inquiries about this opportunity, please contact Search Committee Co-chairs: Dr. Jocelyn Bolin, jebolin@bsu.edu Dr. Ophelie Desmet, ophelie.desmet@bsu.edu Important: Please follow upload instructions for attaching all required documents listed below. Only complete applications will be considered. REQUIRED APPLICATION DOCUMENTS: Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Agenda Within the application, please provide names and contact information for three (3) professional references. Note: Additional application materials may be requested later in the search process This position will remain open until filled, with a consideration date of October 28, 2026. Candidates submitting application materials on or before this date will receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Food-Concept-Group-Leader_R-01359": {
      "title": "Food Concept Group Leader",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Food Concept Group Leader Compensation: $19.24 - $19.24 Department: Ball State University Dining_H Start Date: 08/07/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Dining has an opportunity for a Group Lead position. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefit package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, University-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more! The ideal candidate will possess great customer service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on-campus opportunity. Hours: (Two week) Sunday: Off Monday: 1:30p-10p Tuesday: 1:30p-10p Wednesday: 1:30p-10p Thursday: 1:30p-10p Friday: 12:30-9p Saturday: Off Sunday: Off Monday: 1:30p-10p Tuesday: 1:30p-10p Wednesday: 1:30p-10p Thursday: 1:30p-10p Friday: 12:30-9p Saturday: Off Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under the direction of the Unit Manager, lead, direct, and assist employees in achieving excellence in customer satisfaction, food quality, service of food, employee efficiency and productivity, compliance with safety and sanitation standards,  HACCP standards, Indiana Food Service Code regulations, and rules, policies and procedures of Ball State University. Additional functions include but are not limited to record keeping, physical inventory, subordinate training, communication, executing promotions and advertisements, complying with branded concept license and franchise agreements and standards of operations, executing detailed plans and arrangements, contributing to menu, recipe, and concept development, and participating in preparation and serving of food or cashiering.' Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Perform food preparation, service, and cashiering duties when assigned. Requires the physical ability to walk, push, pull, climb, crouch, reach, stoop, feel, finger, stand for an extended period of time, possess dexterity and strength in the hands, arms, and shoulders, and exert up to 35 pounds of force unassisted. Task requires visual ability to read stem thermometer, menu and computer records, distinguish color, perceive depth, etc. Task requires ability to use all beverage machines, toaster, ice cream machines, ice dispenser, salad bar, food warmer, glassware and china dispenser, serving utensils, rubber, plastic and latex gloves, and all other food service equipment. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions, noise, extreme heat, etc. Task requires mental ability to perform basic mathematical calculations, to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information, and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   2. Lead, direct, and assist employees in the correct and timely procedures in meeting license/franchise and department standards in relation to the preparation and service of all menu items including but not limited to recipe preparation, food presentation, quality control, customer service and sanitation and safety as defined by BSU manuals, handbooks, HACCP standards, Indiana Food Code, NRA ServSafe, and other industry standards. Requires the physical ability to walk, push, pull, climb, crouch, reach, stoop, feel, finger, stand for an extended period of time, possess dexterity and strength in the hands, arms, and shoulders, and exert up to 35 pounds of force unassisted. Task requires visual ability to read stem thermometer, menu and computer records, distinguish color, perceive depth, etc. Task requires ability to use all beverage machines, toaster, ice cream machines, ice dispenser, salad bar, food warmer, glassware and china dispenser, serving utensils, rubber, plastic and latex gloves, and all other food service equipment. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions, noise, extreme heat, etc. Task requires mental ability to perform basic mathematical calculations, to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information, and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   3. Orient, coach, and train employees resulting in well-trained staff that will consistently exhibit excellence in job knowledge and performance; ensure employees are well-trained before working in any job assignment; and provide accurate, balanced feedback to employees regarding job performance. Requires the physical ability to walk, push, pull, climb, crouch, reach, stoop, feel, finger, stand for an extended period of time, possess dexterity and strength in the hands, arms, and shoulders, and exert up to 35 pounds of force unassisted. Task requires visual ability to read stem thermometer, menu and computer records, distinguish color, perceive depth, etc. Task requires ability to use all beverage machines, toaster, ice cream machines, ice dispenser, salad bar, food warmer, glassware and china dispenser, serving utensils, rubber, plastic and latex gloves, and all other food service equipment. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions, noise, extreme heat, etc. Task requires mental ability to perform basic mathematical calculations, to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information, and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   4. Count the safe and audit safe records; audit cashier reports and submit thorough, accurate, cashier check-out reports to bookkeeper; properly report and account for shortages in safe or deposits of sales; complete documentation, report all unaccounted monies (over $20.00) immediately to the Unit Manager; check and approve all cashier refunds to customers and audit the No Sale transactions of each cashier in order to prevent cashier theft; maintain accurate and up-to-date meal card system, including but not limited to reporting lost cards, verifying account status, and overseeing the recording of offline transactions; administer university and departmental policies as related to money handling and reporting; ensure cahiers properly ring sales to record product movement and product value related to each brand upon which royalty payments to brand licensors or franchisers are based. Requires the physical ability to grasp, push, pull, stoop, crouch, reach, walk, stand, lift, feel, have dexterity and strength in hands, and exert up to 20 pounds of force occasionally, and up to 10 pounds of force frequently. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth, etc. Task requires the ability to use computerized card reader, cash register, terminals, calculators, scales, etc. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to perform basic mathematical functions, analyze situations, receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information, and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   5. Scrutinize inventory levels, and other indicators; manage purchasing assignment and following policies and procedures of Ball State University; maintain appropriate inventory levels of foods and supplies as assigned, with neither being over or under-stocked; complete weekly inventory of foods and supplies with a high degree of accuracy. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, reach, push, pull, grasp items, lift arms overhead and stack stock 6 feet high, operate flat bed skid, dolly, various carts several times during work shift, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the ability to write food amounts and the visual ability to read labels, directions and warnings, distinguish color, perceive depth, etc. Task exposes employee to inside and outside environmental conditions, including freezer conditions. Task requires the ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information, and understand and apply universal precautions.   6. Oversee and maintain adequate staffing following University procedures to schedule replacement employees; complete documentation related to scheduling regular and overtime staff; maintain confidentiality and ethical practices relating to communications. Requires the physical ability to use a computer, telephone, and communicate with employees; requires mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information, and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   7. Unlock facility for the day’s operations and secure the facility for the periods of closure; observe safety and security precautions to prevent personal or employee injury, and theft of university or employee property; maintain personal and unit keys in a safe manner to prevent unauthorized use. Requires the physical ability to stoop, kneel, reach, walk, stand, push, pull, grasp, and exert up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, up to 25 pounds of force frequently, and up to 10 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth. Task requires the ability to grasp, handle, and use keys, allen wrench, etc. Task exposes employee to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to be attentive to detail and precise directions.   8. Assist in optimizing profitability through effective monitoring and supervision of food waste, portion control, inventory management, key control, theft and security controls, correct and accurate use of the POS register, carful care for the facility, equipment and furnishing; assist in evaluating food, labor and other controllable costs; implement corrective measures as needed. Requires the physical ability to walk, push, pull, climb, crouch, reach, stoop, feel, finger, stand for an extended period of time, possess dexterity and strength in the hands, arms, and shoulders, and exert up to 35 pounds of force unassisted. Task requires visual ability to read stem thermometer, menu and computer records, distinguish color, perceive depth, etc. Task requires ability to use all beverage machines, toaster, ice cream machines, ice dispenser, salad bar, food warmer, glassware and china dispenser, serving utensils, rubber, plastic and latex gloves, and all other food service equipment. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions, noise, extreme heat, etc. Task requires mental ability to perform basic mathematical calculations, to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information, and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   9. Assist in executing an effective marketing and promotion program for the unit in conjunction with the Unit Manager. Requires the visual ability to read computer records, distinguish color, perceive depth, etc.; requires mental ability to perform basic mathematical calculations, to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information, and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   10. Assist in planning of standard and custom menus, submit recipes for new menu items, and assist with development of sales mix for the unit; assist in planning and executing special events, catered events, and other non-routine food services. Requires the visual ability to read menu and computer records, distinguish color, perceive depth, etc; requires mental ability to perform basic mathematical calculations, to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information, and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information.   11. Perform other duties as assigned.   Minimum Qualifications: 1. High School diploma or equivalent (GED). 2. Two (2) years of direct or related work experience in food service. 3. Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures. 4. You must be 18 years or older. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Additional experience in food service. 2. Supervisory experience with demonstrated leadership and team building skills. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact:    University Dining at 765-285-1967. Please follow upload instructions to attach any supporting documents. NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume . What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Schedule-Specialist-and-Academic-Affairs-Coordinator_R-03198": {
      "title": "Schedule Specialist and Academic Affairs Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Schedule Specialist and Academic Affairs Coordinator Compensation: $16.50 - 17.84 Department: College of Health Deans Office_A Start Date: 10/26/2026 About this opportunity: College of Health | Ball State University The Ball State University College of Health is seeking a highly organized and detail-oriented Scheduling Specialist and Academic Affairs Coordinator to join the Dean's Office team. This position plays a vital role in supporting the academic and operational success of the College through course scheduling, faculty workload management, academic affairs coordination, and technology support. Key Responsibilities: -Coordinate and manage course scheduling for the College of Health. -Oversee faculty load assignments and compensation processes. -Allocate and manage classroom space to support instructional needs. -Administer affiliation agreements and contracts. -Support program accreditation, assessment, and reporting activities. -Ensure data integrity and assist with data management processes. -Coordinate technology-related needs within the College. -Train and support college staff on scheduling and faculty load procedures. The Scheduling Specialist and Academic Affairs Coordinator provides operational support and coordination in two primary areas: course scheduling and academic affairs administration. This role serves as a key resource for faculty, staff, and administrators by ensuring accurate scheduling, effective space utilization, compliance with accreditation requirements, and reliable data reporting. This is an excellent opportunity for a collaborative individual who enjoys working in a dynamic academic environment and contributing to student and faculty success. Join the College of Health at Ball State University and make an impact through effective coordination, organization, and support of academic operations. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: The College of Health (COH) Dean's Office requires operational support and coordination in two main areas. First, as a Schedule Specialist, responsibilities include course scheduling, managing faculty load and compensation processes, and allocating classroom space. Second, in Academic Affairs Coordination, the role involves managing affiliation agreements and contracts, supporting program accreditation and assessment, ensuring data integrity and reporting, and coordinating technology. Additionally, this position includes training college staff on scheduling and faculty load procedures. Duties & Responsibilities: Schedule Specialist Related: Enter schedules and FLAC into Banner, working directly with department chairpersons and department administrative coordinators. Provide relevant data to the Associate Dean in preparation for review and oversight of schedules, course enrollment, faculty assignments, and compensation. Review, correct, and monitor the schedule of course offerings, course modality, past and current enrollments, credit hours, term dates, day and time configurations, section limits/caps, and room attributes and assignments, in consultation with department chairs, administrative coordinators, and the Associate Dean. Be aware of, and adhere to, important semester and academic deadlines, including semester course roll schedules, final course build deadlines, and priority and open registration dates. Communicate information to academic units within the college. Collaborate with the College Budget Director to maintain data in the Faculty Load and Compensation (FLAC) system Train new staff (department chairpersons, administrative coordinators, and other department staff) within COH concerning scheduling and faculty load process and policies. Provide support to Series 25 classroom space allocation and utilization software. Academic Affairs Coordinator Related: Coordinate the development, renewal, routing, execution, and maintenance of affiliation agreements, memoranda of understanding (MOUs), and other college-related contracts Coordinate annual technology and equipment requests on behalf of the college with university Information Technology and the Office of the Provost. Coordinate college assessment processes, including collecting and organizing annual assessment reports submitted by departments/schools, and providing administrative support for academic unit reviews. Support college program accreditation activities, including maintaining accurate records of program accreditation status and history, and providing administrative support to departments/schools undergoing accreditation or reaccreditation. Perform data integrity checks to ensure accuracy of academic affairs-related data in Banner. Assist the Dean and Associate Dean for Academic Affairs with data requests. Act as College Data Liaison with the Office of Institutional Research and Decision Support. General: Perform other related duties as assigned. Maintain regular and predictable attendance.    Minimum Qualifications: Associate's degree or equivalent. At least one year of office administrative, secretarial, or related experience. Excellent communication skills. Working knowledge of word processing & database management software; including common skill sets with Microsoft Office product and database management training. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree. Some experience using Banner and R25. Familiarity with Degree Works. Familiarity with academic procedures and college calendars. Strong communication skills. Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively. How to apply: Inquiries may be directed to Dr. Jakob Lauver at jake.lauver@bsu.edu The following documents are required in this application: 1. Cover letter 2. Resume (Do not use the Autofill resume feature.) Applications must be received before 12:01AM on October 6, 2026. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Instructor-of-Music--Graduate-Music-History-_R-03280": {
      "title": "Instructor of Music (Graduate Music History)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Instructor of Music (Graduate Music History) Compensation: $3,000-$9,000 Department: School of Music - Temp Start Date: 01/11/2027 About this opportunity:   Ball State is seeking to hire one adjunct to teach a graduate music history course in the Spring 2027 semester . Qualifying candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: Ball State is seeking to hire one adjunct to teach a graduate music history course in the Spring 2027 semester . This course will meet one time per week on campus for 3 hours, likely during the early evening, or during the day. However, a live zoom might be possible. The instructor will propose a topic. The enrollment in the course will not exceed 15. Qualifications: A doctorate in music history/musicology Review of applications will start: 10/1/2026 How to apply:   Interested instructors should contact Dr. Heather Platt, Area Coordinator for Music History, hplatt@bsu.edu, for information about the position. Requires successful completion of a background check and education verification. Required Documents: Cover letter Resume Three references should be provided"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Temporary-Emens-Laborer_R-01326": {
      "title": "Temporary Emens Laborer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Temporary Emens Laborer Compensation: $18.50 Department: Emens Auditorium - Temp Start Date: 01/12/2026 About this opportunity:   Emens Auditorium is seeking temporary laborers to work events. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Description: This position is for stage hands that will be responsible for loading and unloading equipment trucks and will work setting up and tearing down of production items on upcoming events performing at Emens Auditorium, Pruis Hall, and Brown Family Amphitheatre. This position may include work with hair and make-up, audio, property crew, and follow spot operators. Electrical and carpentry work may also be needed. Job Responsibilities and Duties: This position is for a wide variety of functions that is necessary for putting on a live production before an audience. Minimum Qualifications: High School graduate or equivalent (GED). Ability to lift up to 75 pounds. Position requires extended periods of standing and physical laborer. ​ Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. Requires successful completion of a background check. Preferred Experience: Over 3 months of related experience. Experience in carpentry, electrical, follow spot operator, property crew, audio crew, truck loaders, pushers, backline, costumes, hair/make-up crew, and video crew. How to apply:   Required Documents: Optional Resume and Cover Letter outlining your previous work experience. Immediate positions are available."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Dean-of-Media-and-General-Manager-of-BSU-Public-Media_R-03259": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean of Media and General Manager of BSU Public Media",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Dean of Media and General Manager of BSU Public Media Compensation: $100,000 - $120,000 Department: CCIM Deans Office About this opportunity: Ball State University is seeking a collaborative and forward-thinking leader to serve as Assistant Dean of Media and General Manager of BSU Public Media. Reporting to the Dean of the College of Communication, Information, and Media, this position provides strategic leadership for Indiana Public Radio and Ball State PBS while supporting the college's academic mission. The successful candidate will oversee public media operations, digital innovation, financial stewardship, fundraising, community engagement, and FCC compliance. As a member of the CCIM leadership team, this individual will also contribute to student success through teaching and oversight of experiential learning opportunities, including the Public Media Accelerator Program. This is an exceptional opportunity to shape the future of public media, strengthen community connections, and prepare the next generation of media professionals. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Reporting to the Dean of the College of Communication, Information, and Media (CCIM), the Assistant Dean and General Manager oversees the strategic, operational, and digital transformation of BSU Public Media. The General Manager builds an integrated content ecosystem—encompassing broadcast, streaming, podcasting, web, and mobile platforms—to expand news delivery, tell community stories, and grow audience engagement across East Central Indiana and statewide. As Assistant Dean of Media and General Manager of BSU Public Media, this leader will also fully participate in the college leadership team and support CCIM’s Academic Mission. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in communications, business, or related field by date of employment. Minimum of 5 years of media/broadcast management with demonstrated leadership in budgeting, fundraising, and team building. Expertise in digital-first distribution, audience analytics, public speaking, FCC regulatory governance, and cross-platform newsroom operations and content creation. Preferred Qualifications: A terminal degree in communications, business, or a related field. Preferred 7+ years in public media leadership and 2 years in a university setting. Duties & Responsibilities: Integrated Ecosystem Leadership: Provide strategic direction that unifies Indiana Public Radio and Ball State PBS into an agile, cross-platform news and content operation designed to meet evolving audience media consumption habits. Audience Development & Community Engagement: Cultivate relationships with civic, business, and community leaders to expand public support, elevate brand awareness, and deepen multi-platform audience engagement. Resource Management & Revenue Diversification: Manage station budgets, funds, grants, and financial forecasting. Drive growth through cross-platform underwriting, major gift development and stewardship, membership strategies, and non-profit fundraising. Technology Infrastructure & Emerging Media Distribution: Partner with the college and University Media Services Chief Engineer to lead the acquisition, implementation, and lifecycle management of core technical infrastructure and emerging distribution technologies. Strategically allocate resources to maintain modern production facilities and build an agile, cross-platform media ecosystem that powers seamless broadcast, digital, and streaming delivery for our audience. Student Experiential Learning & Pedagogy: Assist in leading the Public Media Accelerator Program and co-curricular media initiatives. Teach 9 credit hours annually within CCIM. Organizational Leadership, Talent Development & Strategic Operations: Provide strategic leadership for BSU Public Media's workforce and daily operations by supervising key department leaders, guiding talent acquisition and development, overseeing performance and compensation practices, and ensuring HR compliance. Foster an inclusive, high-performing culture that supports employee growth and organizational success while maintaining an active, visible presence across Public Media and CCIM to strengthen collaboration, build community, and drive operational excellence. Statewide Innovation & News Collaboration: Partner with CCIM, Indiana broadcasting stations, and regional news outlets to pioneer collaborative media creation & delivery models that strengthen local journalism across the station. Regulatory Compliance & Next-Gen Infrastructure: Ensure full FCC compliance and manage licensing for stations WBST 92.1FM in Muncie, WBSB 89.5 FM in Anderson, WBSW 90.0 FM in Marion, WBSH 91.1 FM in Hagerstown, and WIPB-TV Channel 49 in Muncie for Ball State University. Collaborate with FCC legal counsel. Oversee necessary annual reports and licensure renewals. Community Representation & Industry Leadership: Serve as an ambassador and strategic leader representing BSU Public Media, CCIM, and Ball State University across local, state, and national committees, boards, and industry organizations to elevate institutional visibility, shape public media policy, and expand cross-platform partnership opportunities. Operational Adaptability & On-Site Presence: Maintain regular on-site attendance to provide visible, accessible leadership, foster direct collaboration across station teams and campus partners, and execute other related duties as assigned to support the mission of BSU Public Media. Perform other related duties as assigned. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Heather Hines at heather.hines@bsu.edu. Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume: Cover Letter CV/Resume Applications must be received by October 16, 2026, at 12:01 AM.  What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 24 vacation days, 12 sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Professional and download the spreadsheet. If you are applying for a 10-month position or one with Burris or Indiana Academy, please select the corresponding calculator."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Assistant-Lecturer-Assistant-Teaching-Professor-of-Mathematical-Sciences_R-03272": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor of Mathematical Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Lecturer/Assistant Teaching Professor of Mathematical Sciences Compensation: $50,000 - $60,000 Department: Mathematical Sciences Start Date: 08/16/2027 About this opportunity: The Department of Mathematical Sciences is seeking applicants for a full-time non-tenure line faculty position as Assistant Lecturer or Assistant Teaching Professor of Mathematical Sciences (Mathematics Education Specialization) beginning August 16, 2027. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you will bring: Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching approximately 12 credits per term of mathematics education courses and other courses depending on Department need and applicant qualifications, including core curriculum courses such as quantitative reasoning.  Pursue a program of professional development and perform service activities for the Department.  Evidence of high-quality teaching, continuing professional development, and significant service are necessary to be eligible for reappointment. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in mathematics education or closely related field from an accredited institution by date of appointment, with at least 18 graduate semester hours of coursework in mathematics; current or previous teaching licensure or certification; at least two years of K-12 teaching experience. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience at the college level in undergraduate classes.  Doctorate degree in mathematics education with experience or interest teaching online.  Interest in partnerships with local schools.  Demonstrated capacity to work with diverse students as well as to prepare future educators to work with diverse populations.A   How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Dr. Jenna Menke, Search Committee Chair, jenna.menke@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below.  Important:  Do not use the autofill feature for resume. Required documents: Cover letter Teaching philosophy statement Curriculum Vitae Master’s transcript Licenses/certifications Optional documents: Doctoral transcript if applicable Additional materials supporting excellence in teaching Original transcripts showing your highest degree will be required upon hire. Consideration Date: to ensure full consideration, applications must be received by November 6th, 2026. (Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants.) What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer 12 paid sick days and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Faculty and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/PT-Ball-State-Information-and-IT-OCC-Representative_R-03267": {
      "title": "PT Ball State Information and IT OCC Representative",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: PT Ball State Information and IT OCC Representative Compensation: $12.65 - 13.69 Department: Telephone Services Start Date: 10/19/2026 About this opportunity: Join Ball State’s Operations Control Center (OCC) as a part-time, 2nd shift Information and IT operator! In this crucial 24/7 role as a Ball State Information and IT Representative, you’ll provide visitors with accurate information and welcoming directions, monitor vital systems, handle outages, and ensure our campus stays online and connected. Ready to make a real impact? Apply today! Work Shift Schedule: Hours are as follows, with a $0.50 per hour second-shift premium. Thursday-Friday 3:30 pm – 7:30 pm Saturday 9:00 am - 6:00 pm This role requires an on-campus presence; it is not a remote position. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Provide telephone assistance and general information to university offices, faculty, staff, students, and local, regional, national, and international callers. Operate  BSU radio communications. Monitor systems and respond to service-impacting events supported by the Operations Control Center (OCC) by following standardized procedures. Serve as essential personnel as needed.   Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Provide prompt and courteous assistance and information to internal and external callers. This includes telephone numbers, special events and activities, building locations, directions, and emergency information. 2. Perform  ERP checks, server walk-thru, follow documented procedures to complete preventative system health checks. 3. Answer and direct incoming calls in an accurate, efficient, and professional manner, implementing exceptional customer service. 4. Assist callers with questions after the Helpdesk closes on weeknights and over weekends; reset passwords and complete Duo Mobile resets as needed. 5. Operate  BSU radio communication system for critical and non-critical situations. Relay work information to maintenance, University Police, custodial and housing personnel and maintain a log of all radio calls. 6. Continually maintain a working knowledge of events occurring on  BSU Campus and BSU affiliated activities by using Ball State web pages, calendars, department contacts, news articles, as well as Marketing and Communication postings. 7. Respond to and take corrective action in response to system alarms and failures by determining technical priorities based on set standards and procedures. Analyze console messages; use problem/incident notifications and escalation procedures, and other documentation to resolve problems; contact and communicate job and/or system status with applicable System Service team members and support personnel. 8. Monitor and provide security for Operations Control Center and the primary data center in Robert Bell Building. 9. Gather and analyze data to be used for training and staffing purposes. Train new, temporary, and student employees as needed. 10. Serve as essential personnel during severe weather or university crisis situations. 11. Assist Unified Communications technicians in testing lines and numbers during installations and repairs. 12. Perform other related duties as assigned. 13. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or  GED. Over three months through one year of customer service experience.   Preferred Qualifications: Previous call center or Ball State work experience. How to apply: For inquiries, contact Sharee Davis, Operations Control Center Manager, at the following email address: sbconatser@bsu.edu Please list three professional references within the online application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Please follow the upload instructions to attach the required supporting document listed below. Required Document : Resume Optional Document: Cover Letter"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Operations-Coordinator-for-Athletics_R-03295-1": {
      "title": "Operations Coordinator for Athletics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Operations Coordinator for Athletics Compensation: $16.50 - 17.84 Department: Intercollegiate Athletics Ops_F Start Date: 10/19/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State Athletics is seeking an Operations Coordinator for Athletics to support the day-to-day operations of our Olympic Sports programs. This is an excellent opportunity for a highly organized, detail-oriented professional who enjoys working in a fast-paced, team-focused environment and wants to contribute to the success of Ball State's student-athletes and athletic programs. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the United States without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: The Operations Coordinator for Athletics provides administrative and operational support to the athletics department by managing purchasing, budget reconciliation, and travel logistics for designated administrative units. This position plays a critical role in ensuring fiscal accountability, efficient business operations, and exceptional customer service across multiple department functions. The coordinator serves as the primary liaison between assigned units and the athletics business office while supporting executive leadership travel and departmental operational initiatives. This position includes occasional evening and weekend responsibilities related to athletics events and departmental initiatives. Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Coordinate purchasing for assigned athletics units, including Marketing, Communications, Sports Performance, Equipment, and other administrative areas as assigned. 2. Process purchase requisitions, purchase orders, procurement card transactions, invoices, and payment requests in accordance with university and athletics policies. Ensure all purchases comply with university procurement procedures, NCAA regulations, and departmental policies. 3. Reconcile monthly budget activity, identify discrepancies, and work with unit leaders to ensure expenditures are accurate and appropriately documented. 4. Coordinate travel requests for executive staff members and students, including airfare, lodging, ground transportation, and itineraries. 5. Prepare travel authorizations and ensure all required approvals are obtained prior to travel. 6. Reconcile executive travel expenses following completion of travel and submit all required documentation in accordance with university policies. 7. Serve as a resource for travel policies, reimbursement procedures, and expense documentation. 8. Maintain organized financial and travel records for audit and compliance purposes. 9. Assist with year-end budget closeout and fiscal reporting activities. 10. Support department-wide operational initiatives and special projects. 11. Collaborate with campus business offices, procurement, accounts payable, and travel services to resolve financial and operational issues. 12. Develop and maintain effective working relationships with coaches, staff, vendors, and university partners. 13. Receive mail and packages on behalf of the department, then distribute accordingly. 14. Greet all guests entering the Athletics Administrative area. 15. Purchase office supplies on behalf of the Athletics Administrative area and consistently restock items in the Athletic Director’s suite. 16. Perform other duties as assigned to support the mission of the athletics department. 17. Maintain regular and predictable attendance. Minimum Qualifications Associate’s degree or equivalent from an accredited institution. At least one year of experience in athletics administration, operations, or business support. Strong organizational skills with exceptional attention to detail. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Excel. Ability to manage multiple priorities while meeting deadlines. Demonstrated customer service and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in collegiate athletics, higher education, or a business operations environment through internships, graduate assistantships, or full-time employment. Experience with financial systems, purchasing platforms, or travel management software. Knowledge of NCAA, conference, and university financial policies and procedures. How to apply: Please apply via the online Ball State University job portal . Please list three professional references within the online application. Supporting Documents Upload Instructions: Important:  Do  not  use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Required Document: Resume ​ ​Optional Document: Cover Letter What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer paid 10 to 24 vacation days, 12 sick days, and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition.  This offer is good from the very first day you start. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow. Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that show you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Staff (Exempt) and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Temporary-Substitute-Bus-Driver_R-03313": {
      "title": "Temporary Substitute Bus Driver",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPosition Title:   Temporary Substitute Bus Driver Compensation: 20.14 / hour Department: General Institutional Support - Temp Start Date: 10/22/2026 About this opportunity:   Ball State University welcomes applications for Temporary Substitute Bus Drivers. At Ball State University our Temporary Substitute Bus Drivers will operate Ball State University buses to transport students, faculty, staff, and personnel on the shuttle run or other dispatched runs. Work hours and days are as assigned per bus requests. There is no set schedule or shift. Number of hours per week varies; could be 0 hours to 40+ hours a week depending on demands. Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring:   Position Function: Operate Ball State University buses to transport students, faculty, staff, and personnel on the shuttle run or other dispatched runs. Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Operate passenger buses, shuttles, vans and paratransit units on various routes as established by the Transportation Office. 2. Inspect buses and report any equipment malfunctions; maintain cleanliness of vehicles. 3. Fuel daily and inspect bus for any exterior damage. 4. Maintain contact with Transportation Office when necessary via radio and/or telephone; inform office of changes in location, delays, traffic problems, emergencies, etc. 5. Maintain accurate records of mileage and number of passengers; complete various trip sheets and logs for each assigned task. 6. Assist and direct disabled individuals on and off vehicles as needed. 7. Report any problems with routes and make recommendations for changes when appropriate. 8. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1. High School Diploma or Equivalent ( GED ) 2. At least six months of verified professional driving experience. 3. Must demonstrate ability to drive bus (on-site driving test). 4. Must possess and maintain a valid   CDL   (Commercial Driver’s License) with an endorsement for public passengers and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. 5. Must possess a good driving record; verification through Bureau of Motor Vehicles. 6. Must pass a post offer/pre-employment mandatory drug and alcohol test. 7. Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty. Preferred Qualifications: Over-the-road ( OTR ) bus or truck driving experience. How to apply:   For inquiries, please contact: Mike Hill, Supervisor of Bus Operations at 765-285-6005, mdhill5@bsu.edu Please follow upload instructions to attach all of the required supporting documents listed below: NOTE: Do not use the Autofill feature for resume. Cover Letter (optional) Resume"
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Food-Service-Cashier_R-03208-1": {
      "title": "Food Service Cashier",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Food Service Cashier Compensation: $17.29 - $17.29 Department: Student Ctr Tally Food Court_A Start Date: 09/25/2026 About this opportunity: Ball State University Dining has an opportunity for a Cashier position at Starbucks in the Tally. This opportunity comes with excellent pay and a great benefit package that includes medical and prescription plans, dental, flexible spending and health savings accounts, paid time off, holiday pay, University-funded retirement, tuition discounts, and more! The ideal candidate will possess great customer service skills with a willingness to learn. This is a full-time, on-campus opportunity. Hours: (Two week) Sunday: OFF Monday: 11:15a-7:45p Tuesday: OFF Wednesday: 11:15a-7:45p Thursday: 11:15a-7:45p Friday: 11:15a-7:45p Saturday: 8:15a-4:45p Sunday: 8:15a-4:45p Monday: OFF Tuesday: 11:15a-7:45p Wednesday: 11:15a-7:45p Thursday: 11:15a-7:45p Friday: 11:15a-7:45p Saturday: OFF Candidates for searches must have current authorization to be employed in the U.S. without employer sponsorship. What you'll do and what you'll bring: Position Function: Under supervision, perform duties related to collection and recording of monies. Duties & Responsibilities: 1. Count, wrap, and verify money. Keep money and reports secure at all times. Requires the ability to perform basic mathematical calculations, efficiently operate a calculator, read and comprehend written materials, and be detail-oriented. 2. Open on time and maintain published meal service hours. Requires the ability to walk/stand for extended periods of time. Task requires the visual ability to direct customers to key areas. Employee is exposed to inside environmental conditions. 3. Operate electronic terminals with a high degree of accuracy in logging on, completing cash transactions, completing cash equivalency and debit account transactions, and generating a detailed daily media report at the end of each meal. A high degree of accuracy is expected. Requires the physical ability to grasp, push, pull, stoop, crouch, reach, walk, stand, lift, feel, have dexterity and strength in hands, and exert up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and 10 pounds of force frequently. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth. 4. Prepare a manual ‘Check Out Form’ to report all monies from sales and to account for sales ‘overage’ and ‘shortage’. Form must be neatly written and completely accurate. Frequent overage or shortage is not acceptable. Requires the ability to read and comprehend written materials, perform basic mathematical calculations, grasp and handle objects, and be detail-oriented. Task requires the ability to provide written instructions and information. 5. Customer transactions must be made speedily; interact with customers with a smile, courtesy, friendliness, and helpfulness, and communicate customer concerns, questions, comments, and compliments to supervisor. Requires the ability to use computerized card reader, cash register, terminals, calculators, and scales. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow and provide oral instructions. 6. Maintain cash terminal, scales (where applicable), and other equipment in good condition through correct operation and cleaning procedures. Report equipment malfunctions immediately. Requires the ability to read and comprehend written materials and efficiently operate computerized machinery. Task requires the physical ability to grasp, push, pull, stoop, crouch, reach, walk, stand, lift, feel, and have dexterity and strength in hands. 7. Maintain cleanliness, neatness, attractive product display, and good organization of all areas around and including cashier station. May require any of the above-mentioned abilities . 8. Enforce all rules and regulations, including but not limited to: observation of the servery, dining room and grocery areas for possible theft such as pocketing food items or not paying; In all-you-care-to-eat locations, admit only those who have a valid meal plan or who have paid; Permit carry-out according to policy and procedures; Report all violations immediately to management. May require any of the above-mentioned abilities. 9. May be required to: wash and clean dining room conveyors, tables, chairs, service areas, other furnishings, window sills, plants, and equipment located in dining room, serve or re-supply food, snack foods, and other items, instruct dining room attendants in performance of work, assist with special meals or events, i.e., napkin folding, draping and skirting tables, placing decorations, dishing foods, setting up buffet tables, etc., and launder, dry, fold, hang, and store shirts, towels, skirting, or other dining service items as assigned. Requires the physical ability to grasp, push, pull, stoop, crouch, reach, walk, stand, lift, feel, have dexterity and strength in hands and exert up to 35 pounds of force unassisted. Task requires the ability to receive, comprehend, follow and provide oral instructions. 10. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1.Successful completion of Cashier Training Class and passing score on final test is required for positions with cashiering duties. 2.Must have clean body, teeth, hair, nails, and clothing. 3.No allergies to soaps, cleaning agents, oven cleaners, or other materials or environmental factors in food service, e.g., steam, dust, etc. 4.Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, and University policies, procedures, and communications. 5.Must be able to communicate effectively both orally and in writing in the English language. 6.Must be able to perform all physical and mental requirements outlined in each job duty/responsibility. 7.You must be 18 years or older. Preferred Qualifications: 1.Previous experience in cashiering and using a computerized cash register. Experience in fast food, snack bar, dairy bar, or similar commercial establishment. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: University Dining at 765-285-1967. Please follow upload instructions to attach any supporting documents.  Important: Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Optional documents (Recommended for best consideration) 1. Resume. 2. Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    },
    "https://bsu.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Ball-State-University/Facil-Landscape-Worker-CDL_R-03237-1": {
      "title": "Facil Landscape Worker CDL",
