ust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 2. O perating heat plant auxiliary equipment (water treatment, feed water pumps, air compressors, valves, emergency power generating equipment, etc.) Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, kneel, crawl, grasp, finger, lift, reach, balance, climb, work with arms and hands extended, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, and scaffolds. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 3.  Performing duties related to the construction, replacement, repair, and maintenance of all types of steam distribution equipment; perform maintenance duties such as pump, turbine, compressor and fan rebuilding. Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, kneel, crawl, grasp, finger, lift, reach, balance, climb, talk, hear, work with arms and hands extended, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, and Heating Plant instrumentation and testing equipment. Employee is exposed inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 4. Performing duties related to the replacement and repair of the boiler furnace refractory; install sludge drying equipment. Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, kneel, crawl, grasp, finger, lift, reach, climb, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate hand tools and Heating Plant instrumentation. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 5. Performing pipe fitting, welding, metal work, rigging, low voltage electrical work, insulating and painting tasks. Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, kneel, crawl, grasp, finger, lift, reach, balance, climb, talk, hear, work with arms and hands extended, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, and Heating Plant instrumentation. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 6. Performing water treatment tests, adding chemicals, maintaining water treatment equipment. Requires the physical ability to climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, crawl, reach, finger, grasp, work with arms and hands extended, and exert up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and up to 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to distinguish color and perceive depth. Task requires the ability to operate hand tools, painting, cleaning, lubricating, and vibration equipment, ladders, scaffolds, and Heating Plant instrumentation and testing equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear filter mask, respirator, and various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 7. Maintaining cleanliness and orderliness of work areas, equipment, and vehicles. Requires the physical ability to stoop, crouch, crawl, kneel, grasp, finger, lift, reach, climb, balance, talk, hear, work with arms and hands extended, and exert in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, 50 pounds of force frequently, and 20 pounds of force constantly. Task requires the visual ability to perceive depth, distinguish color, and align parts and equipment. Task requires the ability to operate hand and power tools, ladders, scaffolds, welding machines, cutting torches, and Heating Plant instrumentation and testing equipment. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions, extreme heat and cold, noise, dust, heights, confined spaces, and may be required to wear various protective clothing and/or equipment. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 8. Acquire and maintain knowledge of various job-related chemicals, environmental concerns, and current technological improvements/advancements. Requires the physical ability to walk, stand, talk, hear, grasp, finger, lift, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to read small print, distinguish color, and perceive depth. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 9. Demonstrate through periodic examination proficiency in all aspects of the operation including but not limited to boiler operation, plant operation and emergency procedures. Requires the physical ability to walk, stand, talk, hear, grasp, finger, lift, and exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally. Task requires the visual ability to read small print, distinguish color, and perceive depth. Employee is exposed to inside and outside environmental conditions. Task requires the mental ability to receive, comprehend, follow, and provide oral instructions and information and to read, comprehend, follow, and provide written instructions and information. 10 . Perform other duties as assigned. May require any or all of the above-mentioned abilities. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent (GED ). 1.Successful completion of an apprenticeship program as Stationary Engineer as approved by the Bureau of Apprenticeship and Training, or at least six (6) years of verified proof of experience in operation and maintenance of a gas, and/or oil fired boiler plant or related equipment, or equivalent combination of education and experience from which comparable job knowledge can be acquired as determined by Ball State University. 2.Must possess and maintain a valid Indiana Driver’s License and be insurable under the university’s auto fleet policy. 3.Must be able to read and comprehend all specified policies and procedures for safety, hazardous materials information, University policies, procedures, and communications, and perform mathematical calculations. 4.Must be able to perform all mental and physical requirements as outlined in each job duty/responsibility. 5.You must be 18 years or older. Preferred Qualifications: Vocational school training 1.More than six (6) years of verified proof of experience in operation and maintenance of a gas, and/or oil-fired boiler plant or related equipment. How to apply: For inquiries, please contact: Devon Johnson, Assistant Manager of Plant Operations at 765-285-6176 or devon.johnson@bsu.edu . Important:  Do not use the Autofill feature when uploading your resume. Optional documents (Recommended for best consideration). Resume Cover Letter detailing your qualifications for the position. What we offer: At Ball State University, we understand the importance of balancing professional responsibilities with personal well-being. That's why we offer a generous paid time off program and 10 holidays a year. Plus, our paid parental leave (6 weeks) is there for life's most significant moments. We offer affordable health and dental insurance, robust short-term disability, long-term disability and life insurance plans, as well a range of retirement benefits to provide financial security to you and your family. These benefits ensure that you can focus on your work and personal growth without worrying about the unexpected. When you work for us, you are family. And to show our support of your family, we will cover 90 percent of your child's (or children's) undergraduate college tuition at Ball State. We do the same for you.  In fact, we'll cover 100 percent of the tuition costs for you to earn your undergraduate degree and 80 percent of your graduate tuition. It's just one way we do our part to uplift you. Let's fly together toward a secure and prosperous tomorrow.   Curious about our excellent benefits package? We have developed a calculator that shows you the value of our core benefits. Select the Total Compensation Calculator - Service and download our calculator spreadsheet."
    }
  },
